D('inlet',{
    etymology: {"origin":"1570年代英语 inlet 用于‘海岸向内凹入的狭窄水道或海湾’，是中古英语 inlate 的专门用法；后者来自 inleten‘让……进入’，即 in + let。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inlet"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"地理 · 海岸","senseId":"inlet.s1","en":"The survey team entered the narrow inlet by boat at dawn, where steep cliffs sheltered the water from the strongest waves outside.","zh":"调查队黎明时乘船进入狭窄的海湾入口，陡峭的悬崖保护湾内水域，使其免受外海巨浪冲击。","structure":"The survey team entered the narrow inlet by boat at dawn / where steep cliffs sheltered the water / from the strongest waves outside.","grammar":"inlet 指进入海岸内侧的水道或海湾；where 引导修饰 inlet 的定语从句。","rationale":"这是通向海岸内部的水口，符合来源义 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'At low tide, the narrow inlet became too shallow for the ferry.','退潮时，这条狭窄水湾变得太浅，渡船无法通行。')],mistakes:[m("The rescue boat sailed out of the desert inlet to reach the sheltered water.","The rescue boat sailed into the coastal inlet to reach the sheltered water.","A desert with no sea access has no coastal inlet; sail into is the correct direction for entering a real inlet.")] ,quiz:[q('inlet',1,1,'A narrow inlet cuts into the coastline. What is it?','a narrow water passage or bay entering the land','a hill with no access to the sea','a river flowing away from the coast','inlet 指海岸向陆地凹入形成的水道或小海湾。'),q('inlet',2,1,'A map marks an inlet behind the headland. A boat would find?','a sheltered opening from the sea into the land','a dry mountain pass far inland','a road connecting two towns','海岸地形中的 inlet 是海水进入陆地的入口。'),q('inlet',3,1,'Which phrase uses inlet in its coastal sense?','a tidal inlet','an inland desert inlet with no water','an inlet of mountain snow','tidal inlet 指受潮汐影响的海湾入口。'),q('inlet',4,1,'A small inlet is best distinguished from the open sea because it?','extends inward from a larger body of water','is always a deep ocean trench','contains no connection to water','inlet 是与较大水域相连并向陆地伸入的水口。')]});
D('inmate',{
    etymology: {"origin":"1580年代由 in（内部的）与 mate（同伴）组成，最初指获准住在他人房屋中的人；‘被关押或收容在机构内的人’义到19世纪才有记录。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inmate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"司法 · 羁押","senseId":"inmate.s1","en":"The lawyer reminded the family that an inmate may be awaiting trial, so the word alone does not prove that a person has been convicted.","zh":"律师提醒家属，在押人员可能仍在等待审判，因此 inmate 一词本身并不能证明此人已经被定罪。","structure":"The lawyer reminded the family / that an inmate may be awaiting trial / so the word alone does not prove that a person has been convicted.","grammar":"inmate 指被关押在监狱中的人；may be awaiting 表示可能正在等待，that 引导宾语从句。","rationale":"例句使用监狱中的在押人员义，对应 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'In the old diary, each inmate of the crowded house was listed by name.','在那本旧日记中，拥挤房屋里的每位同住者都被逐一记下姓名。')],mistakes:[m('The prison held inmate during the flood.','The prison held an inmate during the flood.','inmate 是可数单数名词，此处作 hold 的宾语时需要限定词 an。')],quiz:[q('inmate',1,1,'A newspaper says an inmate escaped from a prison. The person was?','being held in the prison','visiting the prison for a tour','working outside the prison as a guard','inmate 的常见义是监狱中的在押人员。'),q('inmate',2,2,'The hospital arranged activities for its long-term inmates. Here they are people?','living in the institution and receiving care','sentenced by a court to work there','who own the hospital building','来源也收录机构内住院或被收容者这一义。'),q('inmate',3,3,'In an old account, “the inmates of the house” refers to?','the people who lived in that house','the people who built the house','the visitors who left before entering','旧用法 inmate of a house 指同住者。'),q('inmate',4,1,'Which statement preserves the distinction between charge and conviction?','An inmate may be held before a trial has ended.','Every inmate has already been convicted of every alleged crime.','An inmate is always a prison employee.','inmate 表示被关押或收容的人，本身不说明是否已定罪。')]});
D('inn',{
    etymology: {"origin":"Old English inn 意为‘住宿处、住宅’，可能来自 inne（里面、内部）；‘提供住宿的酒馆’义约在中世纪后期形成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inn"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"旅行 · 住宿","senseId":"inn.s1","en":"The hikers booked an inn beside the old road because it offered both a warm meal and a quiet room after a long day on the trail.","zh":"徒步者预订了旧路旁的一家小旅馆，因为走了一整天山路后那里既能提供热饭，也有安静的房间。","structure":"The hikers booked an inn beside the old road / because it offered both a warm meal and a quiet room / after a long day on the trail.","grammar":"inn 在这里指可住宿和用餐的小旅馆；both…and…连接两项服务。","rationale":"旅店提供住宿与用餐，符合 s1 的小旅馆义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The villagers gathered at the inn to hear the traveling musicians.','村民聚在酒馆里听巡回演奏者演奏。')],mistakes:[m("The travelers booked inn beside the old road for the night.","The travelers booked an inn beside the old road for the night.","Inn is a singular count noun here and needs the article an.")],quiz:[q('inn',1,1,'Travelers stayed overnight at a country inn. It was most likely?','a small lodging house','a railway station','a private farm with no guests','inn 常指乡间的小旅馆或客栈。'),q('inn',2,2,'The villagers met at the inn for a drink. In this sentence it is?','a pub or tavern','a hospital ward','a court building','inn 也可指酒馆或小酒吧。'),q('inn',3,1,'Which preposition fits the usual lodging phrase? “They stayed ___ an inn.”','at','on','by to','表示住在某家旅店常用 stay at an inn。'),q('inn',4,2,'The village inn closed its bar at midnight. What closed?','the local pub','a room in a hospital','the entrance to a cave','bar 语境表明 inn 取酒馆义。')]});
D('innate',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪初来自晚期拉丁语 innatus‘生来具有的’，是 innasci‘在……之中出生、起源’的过去分词，构成含 in-‘在内’与 nasci‘出生’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/innate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"发展 · 天赋","senseId":"innate.s1","en":"Children show an innate curiosity about how things work, although patient explanations and hands-on practice still help that curiosity grow.","zh":"孩子对事物如何运作有天生的好奇心，不过耐心讲解和亲手实践仍能帮助这种好奇心发展。","structure":"Children show an innate curiosity about how things work / although patient explanations and hands-on practice / still help that curiosity grow.","grammar":"innate 修饰 curiosity；although 引导让步从句，how 引导 curiosity 的内容。","rationale":"好奇被描述为生来就有、并非后天学得，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The researchers tested whether fear of certain sounds is innate or learned.','研究人员测试人们对某些声音的恐惧是天生的还是后天习得的。')],mistakes:[m('The skill was innate because she acquired it only after years of formal lessons.','The skill was learned because she acquired it only after years of formal lessons.','多年正式学习后才获得的技能不是天生的；将 innate 改成 learned 是最小修正。')],quiz:[q('innate',1,1,'An innate ability is one a person?','is born with','learns only through later practice','receives as a written instruction','innate 表示生来具有而非后天学来的。'),q('innate',2,1,'Which is most naturally described as innate in a newborn?','a basic reflex present from birth','the ability to read a map','knowledge of a foreign language','出生时已有的反射符合 innate 的定义。'),q('innate',3,1,'“The team has an innate sense of rhythm” suggests that the sense?','seems natural rather than taught','was memorized from a manual yesterday','is impossible to observe','innate 强调自然具有，通常与学习相对。'),q('innate',4,1,'Choose the closest synonym in “innate curiosity.”','inborn','temporary','imposed','inborn 与 innate 都表示天生的。')]});
D('inner',{
    etymology: {"origin":"约1400年来自古英语 inra，是 inne（在里面）的比较级形式；该词后来可指物体较里面的部分，也引申为精神或情感内部。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inner"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"心理 · 情感","senseId":"inner.s2","en":"After several difficult conversations, he finally admitted his inner fear of disappointing the people who had trusted him.","zh":"经过几次艰难的谈话后，他终于承认自己内心深处害怕辜负那些信任他的人。","structure":"After several difficult conversations / he finally admitted his inner fear / of disappointing the people who had trusted him.","grammar":"inner 修饰 fear，表示内心的；admit + 名词表示承认某种感受。","rationale":"这里指精神和情感内部的恐惧，对应 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The inner of the two rings was made from softer gold.','两枚戒指中靠内侧的那枚由较软的黄金制成。')],mistakes:[m('The inner room faced the garden because it was the room farthest outside the house.','The outer room faced the garden because it was the room farthest outside the house.','farthest outside 与 inner（内部的）矛盾；换成 outer 可保留原意。')],quiz:[q('inner',1,1,'The inner door is beyond the outer door. It is?','farther inside','closer to the street','outside the building','inner 的空间义是内部的、靠里的。'),q('inner',2,2,'After months of reflection, he felt inner peace. This peace was?','a feeling within his mind','a quiet room in the building','a rule imposed by the court','inner peace 指内心或精神上的平静。'),q('inner',3,3,'In “the inner of the two lanes,” inner identifies?','the one nearer the center','the one farthest from the center','both lanes together','词条还收录名词用法 the inner，指两者中靠内的一边。'),q('inner',4,1,'Which pairing contrasts the spatial senses correctly?','inner room / outer wall','inner room / inside wall as opposites','inner room / internal room as opposites','inner 和 outer 分别表示内部与外部。')]});
D('innkeeper',{
    etymology: {"origin":"1540年代由 inn + keeper 构成，意为经营或照看旅店的人；keeper 是 keep 的施事名词。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/innkeeper"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"旅行 · 接待","senseId":"innkeeper.s1","en":"The innkeeper kept a lantern burning by the entrance and helped late arrivals carry their bags upstairs without waking the other guests.","zh":"客栈老板让门口的灯笼一直亮着，还帮晚到的客人把行李搬上楼，没有吵醒其他住客。","structure":"The innkeeper kept a lantern burning by the entrance / and helped late arrivals carry their bags upstairs / without waking the other guests.","grammar":"innkeeper 指经营或照看小旅馆的人；help sb. do 与 without + -ing 分别表示帮助和避免某事。","rationale":"人物负责旅店接待和照料住客，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The innkeeper kept a lamp burning for guests delayed by the snow.','客栈老板为因大雪耽搁的客人留着一盏灯。')],mistakes:[m('The innkeeper rented a room for the night, then checked the guests in at the desk.','The guest rented a room for the night, then checked in at the desk.','租房并办理入住的是客人；innkeeper 是经营旅店的人。')],quiz:[q('innkeeper',1,1,'An innkeeper is responsible for?','running or managing an inn','guarding a prison cell','guiding ships into a harbor','innkeeper 指经营或管理小旅店的人。'),q('innkeeper',2,1,'Guests asked the innkeeper for an extra blanket. They asked?','the person in charge of the lodging','another guest who had just arrived','the town’s harbor pilot','旅客会向旅店经营者提出住宿需求。'),q('innkeeper',3,1,'Which word names a person, rather than a place?','innkeeper','inn','inns','innkeeper 由 inn 与 keeper 构成，指人。'),q('innkeeper',4,1,'A sign says “Ask the innkeeper about breakfast.” Who should answer?','the person who runs the small hotel','a passerby with no link to it','the building itself','innkeeper 是客栈老板或店主。')]});
D('innocent',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪中期经古法语 inocent 来自拉丁语 innocentem‘无害、无罪’，由否定前缀 in- 与 nocentem（nocere‘伤害’的现在分词）构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/innocent"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"沟通 · 无恶意","senseId":"innocent.s3","en":"Her innocent question about the locked cabinet embarrassed no one, because she genuinely did not know that the papers inside were confidential.","zh":"她无心询问上锁柜子的事，并没有让任何人难堪，因为她确实不知道里面的文件属于机密。","structure":"Her innocent question about the locked cabinet embarrassed no one / because she genuinely did not know / that the papers inside were confidential.","grammar":"innocent 修饰 question，表示没有伤害他人的意图；because 引出原因。","rationale":"提问不带恶意，也非蓄意造成伤害，符合 s3。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(4,'The inquiry cleared several innocents who had been blamed for the theft.','调查为几名被指责盗窃的无辜者洗清了嫌疑。')],mistakes:[m('The court found the witness innocent, then convicted him of the same charge.','The court found the witness guilty, then convicted him of the same charge.','对同一指控，判定无罪与定罪相矛盾；只将 innocent 改为 guilty。')],quiz:[q('innocent',1,1,'A defendant found innocent of a charge is?','not guilty of that offense','the person who filed the charge','automatically guilty of another offense','sense 1 指在某项指控中无罪、清白。'),q('innocent',2,2,'An innocent child may believe a harmless story because the child is?','naive or inexperienced','deliberately dishonest','legally responsible for the story','innocent 可形容涉世未深、天真的人。'),q('innocent',3,3,'An innocent remark is one that?','was not intended to hurt anyone','was designed to threaten someone','has been ruled illegal by a judge','sense 3 强调话语没有伤害他人的恶意。'),q('innocent',4,4,'“The innocent were protected during the evacuation” means?','people who were not guilty or involved','the people who organized the crime','the officials who issued the order','the innocent 可作名词，指无辜者。')]});
D('innovate',{
    etymology: {"origin":"16世纪40年代来自拉丁语 innovatus（innovare 的过去分词），innovare 意为‘更新、革新’，由 in-‘进入’与 novus‘新的’构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/innovate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"教育 · 教学法","senseId":"innovate.s1","en":"The school chose to innovate by replacing long lectures with short demonstrations and guided projects that let students test ideas themselves.","zh":"学校决定进行教学革新，用简短演示和指导性项目取代冗长讲授，让学生亲自检验想法。","structure":"The school chose to innovate / by replacing long lectures with short demonstrations and guided projects / that let students test ideas themselves.","grammar":"innovate 表示引入新做法；by + -ing 说明实现革新的方式。","rationale":"学校改变原有教学方式，引入新做法，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The engineers innovated a quieter cooling system for the portable scanner.','工程师为这台便携式扫描仪引入了一种更安静的冷却系统。')],mistakes:[m('The laboratory innovated in a new testing method and introduced it across the clinic.','The laboratory innovated a new testing method and introduced it across the clinic.','innovate in 后接领域；直接接被引入的新方法时去掉 in。')],quiz:[q('innovate',1,1,'A firm that continues to innovate keeps?','introducing new ideas or methods','repeating the same process without change','selling only discontinued products','不及物 innovate 指持续创新或革新。'),q('innovate',2,2,'They innovated a new way to recycle the material. What did they do?','introduced a new method','copied an old rule without change','made the material impossible to use','及物用法 innovate something 表示引入新事物或方法。'),q('innovate',3,1,'Which construction is natural for the “make changes” sense?','innovate in medical technology','innovate at medical technology','innovate to medical technology','来源义项给出的搭配是 innovate in + 领域。'),q('innovate',4,2,'The team innovated a process last year. In this use, innovate is?','a transitive verb with a direct object','a noun meaning an inventor','an adjective describing an idea','innovate a process 中 process 是直接宾语，属及物用法。')]});
D('innovator',{
    etymology: {"origin":"1590年代来自晚期拉丁语 innovator，是 innovare（改变、更新）的施事名词，指引入新变化的人。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/innovator"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"设计 · 发明","senseId":"innovator.s1","en":"The young innovator built a low-cost water filter from locally available materials, then shared the design with neighboring villages.","zh":"这位年轻的创新者用当地现有材料制作了低成本滤水器，随后把设计分享给邻近村庄。","structure":"The young innovator built a low-cost water filter from locally available materials / then shared the design / with neighboring villages.","grammar":"innovator 指提出或引入新做法的人；then 表示随后发生的行动。","rationale":"人物制作并推广新的滤水设计，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The young innovator redesigned the pump so villages could repair it locally.','这位年轻的创新者重新设计了水泵，使村庄能够在当地维修。')],mistakes:[m('The innovator rejected every new method and insisted that the old design could never change.','The traditionalist rejected every new method and insisted that the old design could never change.','坚持拒绝所有新方法的人与 innovator（创新者）相反；traditionalist 更符合描述。')],quiz:[q('innovator',1,1,'An innovator is someone who?','creates or introduces new ideas','only preserves an old system','checks spelling in a finished text','innovator 指创新者或引入新事物的人。'),q('innovator',2,1,'A company calls its engineer an innovator after she develops a new battery. The label praises her?','original contribution','ability to avoid all change','role as a battery customer','开发新型电池体现创新贡献。'),q('innovator',3,1,'Which noun names a person who innovates?','innovator','innovation','innovative','-or 形式 innovator 指实施创新的人。'),q('innovator',4,1,'Choose the closest synonym in “a leading innovator in medicine.”','pioneer','imitator','patient','pioneer 和 innovator 都可指开创者。')]});
D('innumerable',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪中期来自拉丁语 innumerabilis‘数不清的’，由否定前缀 in- 与 numerabilis‘能够计数的’构成，后者来自 numerare‘计数’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/innumerable"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"自然 · 观察","senseId":"innumerable.s1","en":"At night, innumerable insects circled the lamps along the river, making it impossible for the field team to count them reliably.","zh":"夜间，无数昆虫围着河边的灯飞舞，野外小组无法可靠地数清它们。","structure":"At night / innumerable insects circled the lamps along the river / making it impossible for the field team to count them reliably.","grammar":"innumerable 修饰复数名词 insects；making 分词结构说明数量众多造成的结果。","rationale":"数量多到无法逐个计数，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The archive contains innumerable letters from families separated by the war.','档案馆保存着数量极多的战争离散家庭来信。')],mistakes:[m('The report listed exactly three reasons and called them innumerable.','The report listed exactly three reasons and called them few.','exactly three 是有限且可数的少数，不能称为 innumerable；改为 few 即可。')],quiz:[q('innumerable',1,1,'Innumerable stars are stars that?','are too many to count','number exactly five','cannot be seen because there are none','innumerable 的核心义是多到数不清。'),q('innumerable',2,2,'A team faced innumerable difficulties. This means it faced?','a very great number of difficulties','no difficulties at all','exactly one difficulty','该词也可强调困难等数量极多。'),q('innumerable',3,1,'Which phrase is most natural?','innumerable tiny grains of sand','innumerable one grain of sand','an innumerable single grain','innumerable 修饰复数可数对象，表示数量多得无法计数。'),q('innumerable',4,1,'Choose a close synonym for “innumerable opportunities.”','countless opportunities','two opportunities','a rare opportunity','countless 同样表示无数的。')]});
D('inoculation',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪中期先用于园艺中的芽接；医学接种义见于1714年，来自拉丁语 inoculationem，源自 inoculare‘把芽接入植物’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inoculation"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"公共卫生 · 预防","senseId":"inoculation.s1","en":"The clinic recorded each child's inoculation carefully, including the vaccine batch number, so families could check the schedule at their next visit.","zh":"诊所仔细记录每个孩子的接种情况，包括疫苗批次号，以便家人下次就诊时核对接种计划。","structure":"The clinic recorded each child's inoculation carefully / including the vaccine batch number / so families could check the schedule at their next visit.","grammar":"inoculation 指接种行为或接种记录；so 引导目的或结果从句。","rationale":"语境指通过疫苗预防疾病的接种，对应 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'After inoculation, volunteers recorded any fever or soreness for two days.','接种后，志愿者连续两天记录是否发烧或酸痛。')],mistakes:[m("The nurse gave patient an inoculation against measles.","The nurse gave the patient an inoculation against measles.","Patient is a singular count noun and needs a determiner in this sentence.")],quiz:[q('inoculation',1,1,'Inoculation is the act of?','giving a vaccine to help protect against disease','testing whether a room has enough light','removing a vaccine from a patient','来源将 inoculation 释为接种疫苗。'),q('inoculation',2,1,'A public-health notice encourages inoculation before an outbreak. It encourages people to?','receive a protective vaccine','avoid all medical care','spread an infection deliberately','inoculation 是通过接种建立保护的行为。'),q('inoculation',3,1,'Which verb is closely related to inoculation?','inoculate','insulate','insinuate','inoculate 是“给……接种”的动词。'),q('inoculation',4,1,'“Inoculation rates rose” most directly means?','the rate of vaccination increased','more people refused every vaccine','the disease was renamed','rate 修饰的是接种这一行为的发生比例。')]});
D('input',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由英语 in + put 构成；20世纪中期 input 已用作计算机输入的信息，也用于投入的时间、金钱或意见等。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/input"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"治理 · 公众意见","senseId":"input.s3","en":"Before approving the new bus route, the council invited input from commuters who use the station before sunrise and after the evening shift.","zh":"批准新公交线路前，市议会征求了那些日出前和晚班后使用车站的通勤者的意见。","structure":"Before approving the new bus route / the council invited input from commuters / who use the station before sunrise and after the evening shift.","grammar":"invite input from sb. 表示征求某人的意见；who 引导修饰 commuters 的定语从句。","rationale":"通勤者提供意见帮助决策，符合 s3。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The editor asked for input from translators who knew the local dialect.','编辑征求了熟悉当地方言的译者意见。'),ex(4,'She input the measurements before the software generated a chart.','她先输入测量数据，之后软件生成了图表。')],mistakes:[m('The operator input the data onto the database.','The operator input the data into the database.','输入数据进入系统用 input data into；把 onto 改成 into 即可。')],quiz:[q('input',1,1,'A computer rejects an input value. What was rejected?','information entered into the computer','a printed report sent out by the computer','the computer’s power supply','sense 1 是输入计算机的信息或数据。'),q('input',2,2,'A project needs more input of time and money. It needs more?','resources invested in the project','opinions about the final decision','data typed into a keyboard','sense 2 指投入的时间、精力或资金。'),q('input',3,3,'The council asked for residents’ input. It asked for their?','advice or opinions','computer passwords','financial debts','sense 3 是供决策参考的意见或建议。'),q('input',4,4,'He input the results into the database. What did he do?','entered the results as data','removed the results from the database','asked someone to interpret the results','动词 input 表示把数据输入计算机系统。')]});
D('inquire',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪末由古法语 enquerre 或直接来自拉丁语 inquirere‘调查、查问’，由 in-‘进入’与 quaerere‘寻求’构成；英式拼写 enquire 也存在。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inquire"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"服务 · 问讯","senseId":"inquire.s1","en":"Passengers may inquire at the information desk if a platform changes, because the electronic signs do not always update immediately.","zh":"如果站台有变，乘客可以到问讯台询问，因为电子指示牌并不总能立即更新。","structure":"Passengers may inquire at the information desk / if a platform changes / because the electronic signs do not always update immediately.","grammar":"inquire at + 地点表示在某处询问；if 引导条件从句，because 引出原因。","rationale":"乘客向工作人员询问信息，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The board appointed an outside team to inquire into the cause of the outage.','董事会任命了外部团队调查停电原因。'),ex(3,'She inquired of the receptionist whether the clinic accepted walk-ins.','她向接待员询问诊所是否接待未预约者。')],mistakes:[m('The officer inquired into the witness where she had parked.','The officer inquired of the witness where she had parked.','询问某人时可用 inquire of somebody；inquire into 用于调查某事。')],quiz:[q('inquire',1,1,'A traveler inquires about the train schedule. The traveler?','asks for information about it','investigates whether the train company is guilty','writes a schedule for the railway','inquire about 指询问某一事项的信息。'),q('inquire',2,2,'The inspector will inquire into the missing funds. The inspector will?','investigate what happened to the funds','ask the funds to provide directions','enter the funds into a computer','inquire into 表示调查、查究某事。'),q('inquire',3,3,'Which phrase means “ask a person”?','inquire of the receptionist','inquire into the receptionist','inquire at whether the room is free','正式用法可说 inquire of somebody；into 后接调查对象或事件。'),q('inquire',4,1,'A visitor inquires whether the museum is open. The visitor is?','asking to find out a fact','announcing a legal verdict','conducting a scientific experiment','询问开放时间属于 inquire 的问询义。')]});
D('inquiry',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪末经古法语 enquere 或源自拉丁语 inquirere‘探查、寻求’，名词表示询问或查问；美式常见 inquiry，英式亦见 enquiry。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inquiry"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"研究 · 事实核实","senseId":"inquiry.s1","en":"The inquiry began with simple questions about the missing files, but each answer led investigators to a different source that needed checking.","zh":"调查从询问失踪文件的简单问题开始，但每个回答都把调查人员引向另一个需要核实的来源。","structure":"The inquiry began with simple questions about the missing files / but each answer led investigators to a different source / that needed checking.","grammar":"inquiry 作主语，指查问过程；lead sb. to 表示引向，that 从句修饰 source。","rationale":"语境强调为了查明事实而询问，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her inquiry about evening classes led the office to send a course list.','她询问晚间课程后，办公室给她寄来了课程清单。')],mistakes:[m("The board opened an inquiry of the missing funds.","The board opened an inquiry into the missing funds.","The standard collocation is an inquiry into a matter, rather than inquiry of the matter.")],quiz:[q('inquiry',1,1,'A customer makes an inquiry about a refund. The customer makes?','a request for information','a final payment','a complaint that has already been settled','inquiry 可指询问、打听信息。'),q('inquiry',2,1,'After the accident, officials began an inquiry. They began?','an investigation to establish what happened','a celebration for the rescue team','a plan to hide every record','inquiry 也可指正式调查。'),q('inquiry',3,1,'Which verb commonly collocates with inquiry in the investigation sense?','conduct','borrow','decorate','conduct an inquiry 是“开展调查”的常见搭配。'),q('inquiry',4,1,'Several inquiries arrived by email. Here inquiries are?','questions or requests for information','machines used to send email','answers already given','可数 inquiries 可指收到的多个询问。')]});
D('inquisitive',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪末形成，来自拉丁语 inquisitivus 或法语相关形式，关联 inquirere‘查问、探究’；形容爱问问题、好奇探究。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inquisitive"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"博物馆 · 学习","senseId":"inquisitive.s1","en":"An inquisitive child asked how the old clock kept time, then listened closely while the guide explained its gears and swinging pendulum.","zh":"一个好奇爱问的孩子询问那座旧钟如何计时，随后认真听讲解员说明齿轮和摆锤的运作。","structure":"An inquisitive child asked how the old clock kept time / then listened closely / while the guide explained its gears and swinging pendulum.","grammar":"inquisitive 修饰 child；ask how 引导间接疑问，while 表示听讲解时的情境。","rationale":"主动提问以了解更多，符合 s1 的好问义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The inquisitive child asked how the lighthouse lens made distant ships visible.','这个好奇的孩子问灯塔透镜如何让远处的船只变得可见。')],mistakes:[m('The inquisitive reporter refused to ask any questions and showed no interest in the investigation.','The indifferent reporter refused to ask any questions and showed no interest in the investigation.','拒绝提问且毫无兴趣与 inquisitive（好奇、爱探问）相反；indifferent 符合此处。')],quiz:[q('inquisitive',1,1,'An inquisitive student is likely to?','ask questions to learn more','avoid every new subject','already know every answer','inquisitive 指好奇、爱问问题的。'),q('inquisitive',2,1,'An inquisitive look suggests that someone is?','curious about what is happening','angry about a past decision','certain that no answer exists','好奇的神情体现出 inquisitive 的含义。'),q('inquisitive',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym for “an inquisitive mind.”','a curious mind','a careless mind','a silent machine','curious 是 inquisitive 的近义词。'),q('inquisitive',4,1,'Which behavior best fits an inquisitive visitor at a museum?','asking how an ancient tool was used','walking past every exhibit without interest','covering the labels so nobody can read them','主动询问展品用途表现出好奇心。')]});
D('insane',{
    etymology: {"origin":"16世纪末进入英语，来自拉丁语 insanus‘不健康的、失常的’，由 in-‘不’与 sanus‘健康的’构成；口语引申义可指极不明智或疯狂。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insane"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"安全 · 决策","senseId":"insane.s2","en":"Driving across the flooded bridge without checking its depth would be insane, especially when a safe road remains open only ten minutes away.","zh":"不确认水深就开车穿过被淹的桥实在荒唐，尤其是安全道路只在十分钟外仍然开放。","structure":"Driving across the flooded bridge without checking its depth would be insane / especially when a safe road remains open only ten minutes away.","grammar":"insane 在此作表语，评价某个决定极不明智；without + -ing 表示未做某事。","rationale":"冒险行为极不合理，使用 s2 的比喻义，不涉及医学诊断。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The endless alarm is driving the night-shift staff insane.','没完没了的警报快把夜班员工逼疯了。')],mistakes:[m("The engineer called the proposal as insane.","The engineer called the proposal insane.","With call + object + adjective complement, as is not used.")],quiz:[q('insane',1,1,'A person declared insane in a medical or legal context is?','judged to be seriously mentally ill','praised for making a clever plan','temporarily absent from a meeting','sense 1 指被认为患有严重精神疾病。'),q('insane',2,2,'“It would be insane to drive through the flood” means it would be?','extremely foolish or unreasonable','a routine and safe choice','a legally required action','insane 可口语化地形容荒唐、不明智。'),q('insane',3,3,'“The noise is driving me insane” usually means the noise?','is making me extremely annoyed','has formally diagnosed me','is teaching me to operate a machine','口语中 drive someone insane 可表示烦得受不了。'),q('insane',4,2,'Which sentence uses insane as criticism of a decision?','Taking that risk without a helmet is insane.','A court declared the patient insane.','The noise drove the neighbors insane.','第一句评价某种选择荒唐、不明智。')]});
D('inscribe',{
    etymology: {"origin":"约15世纪初来自拉丁语 inscribere‘写在……上、刻上’，由 in-‘在上面/里面’与 scribere‘写’构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inscribe"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"纪念 · 铭刻","senseId":"inscribe.s1","en":"The family asked the mason to inscribe the names of all four volunteers on the stone bench beside the restored community garden.","zh":"这家人请石匠把四位志愿者的姓名刻在修复后的社区花园旁的石凳上。","structure":"The family asked the mason / to inscribe the names of all four volunteers / on the stone bench beside the restored community garden.","grammar":"inscribe A on B 表示把 A 刻写在 B 上；ask sb. to do 表示请求某人做某事。","rationale":"名字被刻在石面上，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The jeweler inscribed the date inside the silver case.','珠宝匠把日期刻在银盒内侧。')],mistakes:[m('The sculptor inscribed the marble plaque by washing all its letters away.','The sculptor cleaned the marble plaque by washing all its letters away.','把字迹全部洗掉是清洁而非铭刻；用 cleaned 替换 inscribed 能保留后半句。')],quiz:[q('inscribe',1,1,'The artist inscribed a name on the stone. The artist?','carved or wrote the name onto it','painted over the stone until no mark remained','measured the stone without marking it','inscribe 指把文字刻写在材料上。'),q('inscribe',2,1,'Which object would most naturally be inscribed?','a memorial tablet','a cloud that leaves no surface','an unwritten thought that is never recorded','铭牌等硬质表面常被刻上文字。'),q('inscribe',3,1,'Choose the correct preposition: “The date was inscribed ___ the ring.”','on','between to','from at','常见结构是 inscribe something on a surface。'),q('inscribe',4,1,'A dedication inscribed inside a book has been?','written or marked there','removed from every page','spoken aloud but not recorded','inscribe 也可指在物品上题写文字。')]});
D('insect',{
    etymology: {"origin":"17世纪初来自拉丁语 insectum‘切成段的东西’，是 insecare（切开）的过去分词，由 in- 与 secare‘切’构成，指身体分节的昆虫。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insect"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"生态 · 识别","senseId":"insect.s1","en":"The guide showed the children how to identify an insect by its six legs, then compared a beetle with a spider that has eight.","zh":"向导教孩子们根据六条腿辨认昆虫，然后把甲虫与有八条腿的蜘蛛作比较。","structure":"The guide showed the children how to identify an insect by its six legs / then compared a beetle with a spider / that has eight.","grammar":"identify an insect by + 特征表示根据特征辨认；how 引导 show 的内容。","rationale":"甲虫以六足等特征归入昆虫，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'He used “insect” as an insult, although the word literally names a small animal.','他用“insect”骂人，尽管这个词字面上指一种小动物。')],mistakes:[m('A bee is an insect with six legs, but it is not an animal.','A bee is an insect with six legs, and it is an animal.','昆虫属于动物；将 but not 改为 and 即可消除分类矛盾。')],quiz:[q('insect',1,1,'Which creature is an insect?','an ant with six legs','a spider with eight legs','a fish with fins','来源所列生物义包括有六条腿的蚂蚁或蜜蜂。'),q('insect',2,2,'If someone contemptuously calls another person an insect, the speaker means?','a contemptible or insignificant person','a respected insect researcher','a person with six literal legs','该词还可贬义地指可鄙或渺小的人。'),q('insect',3,1,'A basic feature of an insect is that it has?','six legs','eight legs','no legs at any stage','来源核心释义将昆虫描述为有六条腿的小动物。'),q('insect',4,1,'Which sentence uses insect literally?','A beetle crawled under the leaf.','The novel calls its villain a miserable insect.','The speaker used insect only as an insult.','甲句指甲虫这种真实昆虫；其余为贬义比喻。')]});
D('insecticide',{
    etymology: {"origin":"19世纪后期由 insect + -cide 构成；-cide 来自拉丁语 caedere‘杀死’，用于表示杀灭某类生物的物质。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insecticide"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"农业 · 害虫控制","senseId":"insecticide.s1","en":"The farmer applied insecticide only to the affected rows and kept the neighboring wildflowers untreated to protect pollinators.","zh":"农民只在受影响的几行作物上施用杀虫剂，邻近野花则未处理，以保护传粉昆虫。","structure":"The farmer applied insecticide only to the affected rows / and kept the neighboring wildflowers untreated / to protect pollinators.","grammar":"apply insecticide to + 范围表示施用杀虫剂；to protect 表示目的。","rationale":"这种药剂用于杀灭或控制害虫，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The label says to keep the insecticide away from children and pets.','标签说明要把杀虫剂放在儿童和宠物接触不到的地方。')],mistakes:[m('The gardener sprayed insecticide to attract more aphids to the roses.','The gardener sprayed insecticide to kill aphids on the roses.','insecticide 用来杀虫而非吸引害虫；将 attract 改为 kill 即可。')],quiz:[q('insecticide',1,1,'An insecticide is a substance used to?','kill or control insects','feed insects so they multiply','measure how fast insects fly','词条释义明确为杀虫的化学品。'),q('insecticide',2,1,'A farmer applies insecticide to a crop because?','insects are damaging the plants','the plants need to attract more pests','the farmer wants to water the soil','使用杀虫剂是为了控制危害作物的昆虫。'),q('insecticide',3,1,'Which broader term can include an insecticide?','pesticide','fertilizer','pollinator','pesticide 是杀虫剂所处的农药类名称。'),q('insecticide',4,1,'“The insecticide was stored safely” most likely means?','the insect-killing chemical was put away carefully','the insects were stored in a safe','the chemical was used as drinking water','insecticide 指杀虫剂，不是昆虫本身。')]});
D('insensitive',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由否定前缀 in- 加 sensitive 构成；sensitive 源自拉丁语 sentire‘感觉、感知’，因此 insensitive 表示感觉或关心较少。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insensitive"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"人际 · 沟通","senseId":"insensitive.s1","en":"His insensitive reply ignored how worried the family was, so the doctor apologized and explained the delay in a more considerate way.","zh":"他那番冷漠的回答没有顾及家人的担忧，于是医生道歉，并以更体贴的方式解释了延误原因。","structure":"His insensitive reply ignored how worried the family was / so the doctor apologized / and explained the delay in a more considerate way.","grammar":"insensitive 修饰 reply；how 引导 ignored 的内容，so 引出后续补救行动。","rationale":"回答没有体察他人的情绪或关切，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'After the injury, the skin around his fingers became insensitive to heat.','受伤后，他手指周围的皮肤对热刺激变得麻木。')],mistakes:[m("The manager was insensitive of the workers' concerns about the schedule.","The manager was insensitive to the workers' concerns about the schedule.","The adjective insensitive takes to before the person or concern affected.")],quiz:[q('insensitive',1,1,'Skin insensitive to pain?','feels little or no pain','feels every touch more strongly than usual','has developed a new sense of smell','insensitive to pain 表示对疼痛感觉迟钝或麻木。'),q('insensitive',2,1,'A person called insensitive in an emotional situation may?','show little care for other people’s feelings','notice and respond gently to every feeling','be unable to hear ordinary sounds','insensitive 还可指不体谅他人感受。'),q('insensitive',3,1,'Which preposition completes the phrase? “insensitive ___ criticism”','to','at of','by for','常用搭配是 insensitive to。'),q('insensitive',4,1,'Which word is closest in meaning to “insensitive to cold”?','numb','curious','generous','对寒冷感觉迟钝近似 numb（麻木的）。')]});
D('insert',{
    etymology: {"origin":"1520年代来自拉丁语 insertus（inserere 的过去分词），inserere 意为‘嫁接、植入’，由 in-‘在里面’与 serere‘连接、排列’构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insert"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"编辑 · 修订","senseId":"insert.s2","en":"The editor asked Nina to insert a short explanation after the chart so readers would understand why the two measurements differed.","zh":"编辑请妮娜在图表后加入一段简短说明，让读者理解两项测量为何不同。","structure":"The editor asked Nina / to insert a short explanation after the chart / so readers would understand why the two measurements differed.","grammar":"insert words/explanation into or after a text 表示在文本中加入内容；why 引导宾语从句。","rationale":"语境是在文章中加入文字，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The editor inserted a short note to explain the historical reference.','编辑插入了一条简短注释来解释这处历史典故。'),ex(3,'A glossy insert advertised the newspaper’s weekend travel section.','一张光面插页为报纸的周末旅游版做了广告。')],mistakes:[m('The editor inserted a note by deleting every sentence from the article.','The editor inserted a note by adding it to the article.','insert 表示加入或放入；全部删掉与插入相反，只将 deleting 改为 adding。')],quiz:[q('insert',1,1,'Insert the card into the slot. What should you do?','put the card into the slot','remove the slot from the machine','write a paragraph on the card','sense 1 是把某物放进另一物中。'),q('insert',2,2,'The editor inserted a paragraph after the introduction. The editor?','added new text to the writing','removed a paragraph from the writing','printed the entire book again','sense 2 指在文章中加入文字。'),q('insert',3,3,'A newspaper includes a color insert. The insert is?','a separate page or section placed inside it','the machine that prints the newspaper','a letter written on the newspaper','名词 insert 可指报刊中的插页。'),q('insert',4,1,'Which phrase follows the common pattern?','insert a coin into the slot','insert a coin across the slot','insert a coin from the slot into','常用结构是 insert A into B。')]});
D('inside',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 in + side 形成，字面是‘在内侧’；中古英语以来可作介词、副词、形容词和名词，具体词类取决于句中位置。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inside"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"场所 · 室内","senseId":"inside.s4","en":"Please wait inside until the storm passes, because the covered entrance is safer than the open courtyard beside the road.","zh":"请先在室内等风暴过去，因为有顶的入口比路边露天庭院更安全。","structure":"Please wait inside until the storm passes / because the covered entrance is safer / than the open courtyard beside the road.","grammar":"inside 在此作地点副词，表示在建筑物里面；until 从句说明等待的时限。","rationale":"说话者要求待在室内，匹配 s4。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(5,'The journalist was given inside information about the company’s planned merger.','记者得到了有关公司计划合并的内部消息。')],mistakes:[m('The key is inside of the box, so you can see it lying on the table outside.','The key is outside of the box, so you can see it lying on the table outside.','钥匙既在盒子里又在盒子外面的桌上，位置互相矛盾；改 inside 为 outside。')],quiz:[q('inside',1,1,'The note is inside the drawer. The note is?','within the drawer','on top of the drawer','under the floor below it','介词 inside 表示在某物内部。'),q('inside',2,2,'“The inside of the tent was dry” uses inside as?','a noun for the inner part','a preposition followed by an object','a verb meaning to close a tent','the inside of 表示某物的内部。'),q('inside',3,3,'An inside pocket is?','a pocket located within a garment','a pocket attached to the outside only','a pocket that cannot hold anything','形容词 inside 表示位于内部或内侧。'),q('inside',4,4,'“It is raining; let us go inside” means?','go into a building or enclosed place','walk farther into the rain','leave the shelter and go outdoors','副词 inside 表示进入室内或内部。')]});
D('insides',{
    etymology: {"origin":"inside 的复数形式；inside 由 in + side 构成，名词复数 insides 常指物体或身体的内部各部分。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inside"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"维修 · 设备","senseId":"insides.s1","en":"The mechanic removed the cracked casing and found rust on the insides of the old pump, where moisture had collected for years.","zh":"机械师拆下开裂的外壳，在旧水泵内部发现了锈迹；那里多年积聚着潮气。","structure":"The mechanic removed the cracked casing / and found rust on the insides of the old pump / where moisture had collected for years.","grammar":"the insides of + 物体指其内部各部分；where 引导修饰 pump 的定语从句。","rationale":"锈迹位于水泵的内部部件，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The mechanic removed the old clock’s insides before cleaning its case.','机械师清洁钟壳前取出了旧钟的内部机件。')],mistakes:[m('He polished the insides of the clock, meaning its painted outer case.','He polished the outside of the clock, meaning its painted outer case.','painted outer case 是外部，不是 insides；只把 insides 改为 outside。')],quiz:[q('insides',1,1,'A machine’s insides are its?','inner parts','painted outer surface','user instructions','insides 是 inside 的复数，指内部各部分。'),q('insides',2,1,'“She felt butterflies in her insides” refers informally to?','sensations in the inner body','the outside of her coat','the machine beside her','该词可口语地指身体内部或内脏。'),q('insides',3,1,'Which verb naturally takes “the insides” as its object?','clean','wear','borrow from','可清洁容器或机器的内部，因此 clean the insides 自然。'),q('insides',4,1,'The word insides is grammatically?','a plural noun','a singular adjective','a verb in the past tense','词条将 insides 收为复数名词。')]});
D('insight',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 in + sight 构成，原义是‘内在的视力、洞察’；英语自16世纪起用来表示理解事物真实本质的能力或由此得到的认识。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insight"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"研究 · 诊断","senseId":"insight.s1","en":"Her insight into the patients' routines helped the team see why the new appointment system caused missed visits in the rural clinics.","zh":"她对患者日常安排的洞察帮助团队发现，新的预约系统为何会导致乡村诊所出现漏诊。","structure":"Her insight into the patients' routines helped the team see / why the new appointment system caused missed visits / in the rural clinics.","grammar":"insight into + 主题表示对某事的洞察；help sb. see 后可接间接疑问从句。","rationale":"她识别了问题背后的真实原因，体现 s1 的洞察力。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The patient gradually gained insight into the symptoms that triggered his panic.','患者逐渐认识到引发自己恐慌的症状。')],mistakes:[m('The book offers no insight into the problem because it explains the problem clearly from several angles.','The book offers insight into the problem because it explains the problem clearly from several angles.','清楚、多角度地解释问题正能提供 insight；删去 no 可消除矛盾。')],quiz:[q('insight',1,1,'A study gives insight into poverty. It helps readers?','understand its nature more deeply','memorize a list of unrelated dates','avoid learning anything about it','sense 1 指深入理解某事本质的能力或认识。'),q('insight',2,2,'A reviewer offers several valuable insights. These are?','deep or useful observations','small holes in a book','rules that prevent discussion','sense 2 可数，指有价值的见解。'),q('insight',3,3,'A patient who lacks insight into an illness?','has little awareness of their own condition','has completed every medical test','has written a report about a hospital','医学义 insight 指对自身病情的自知力。'),q('insight',4,1,'Which phrase is standard?','insight into the causes','insight at the causes','insight for the causes','常见搭配是 insight into。')]});
D('insignificant',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由否定前缀 in- 加 significant 构成；significant 源自拉丁语 significare‘表示、表明’，由 signum‘标记’与 facere‘做’构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insignificant"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"统计 · 结果","senseId":"insignificant.s1","en":"The difference between the two readings was statistically insignificant, so the scientists reported it without claiming that one treatment worked better.","zh":"两次读数之间的差异在统计上微不足道，因此科学家如实报告，但没有声称某种治疗更有效。","structure":"The difference between the two readings was statistically insignificant / so the scientists reported it / without claiming that one treatment worked better.","grammar":"insignificant 修饰 difference；without + -ing 表示报告时没有作出的主张。","rationale":"差异小到不足以支持重要结论，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The difference in weight was insignificant beside the measurement error.','与测量误差相比，这点重量差异微不足道。')],mistakes:[m('The insignificant sum was so large that it paid the entire national debt.','The significant sum was so large that it paid the entire national debt.','足以偿还国债的巨额款项不可能微不足道；改为 significant 即可。')],quiz:[q('insignificant',1,1,'An insignificant change is one that?','is too small to matter','has a major effect on every result','cannot be measured because it is enormous','insignificant 表示小到不重要或微不足道。'),q('insignificant',2,1,'Which amount is most likely insignificant to a large corporation?','one cent in a multibillion-dollar budget','half of its yearly revenue','a payment large enough to prevent bankruptcy','相对于巨额预算，一分钱微不足道。'),q('insignificant',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym for “an insignificant detail.”','a negligible detail','a crucial detail','a well-known detail','negligible 与 insignificant 近义，表示可忽略的。'),q('insignificant',4,1,'If a difference is insignificant, it is usually?','not important enough to affect the conclusion','the most important finding','impossible to compare with anything','该词常表示差异不重要、不影响判断。')]});
D('insincere',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由否定前缀 in- 加 sincere 构成；sincere 经法语来自拉丁语 sincerus‘纯正、真实’，故 insincere 表示感情或表达不真诚。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insincere"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"人际 · 道歉","senseId":"insincere.s1","en":"The apology sounded insincere because he kept checking his phone and never acknowledged the inconvenience his late arrival had caused.","zh":"这番道歉听起来并不真诚，因为他一直看手机，也从未承认迟到给别人造成的不便。","structure":"The apology sounded insincere / because he kept checking his phone / and never acknowledged the inconvenience his late arrival had caused.","grammar":"sound + 形容词表示听起来如何；because 引出判断依据。","rationale":"道歉缺少真诚的态度和承认，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The audience could hear that his apology was insincere because he laughed while making it.','听众听得出他的道歉不真诚，因为他道歉时还在笑。')],mistakes:[m('Her insincere apology expressed genuine regret and was followed by a heartfelt offer to repair the damage.','Her sincere apology expressed genuine regret and was followed by a heartfelt offer to repair the damage.','真诚悔意和发自内心的补救与 insincere（不真诚）冲突；改为 sincere。')],quiz:[q('insincere',1,1,'An insincere compliment is?','not honestly meant','carefully researched and completely accurate','a compliment nobody has heard','insincere 指感情或表达不真诚。'),q('insincere',2,1,'A smile described as insincere may look?','false or forced','warm and fully genuine','unrelated to the person’s feelings in no way','insincere 常指表情或言辞显得虚假。'),q('insincere',3,1,'Which word is the direct opposite of insincere?','sincere','artificial','false','sincere 是 insincere 的反义词。'),q('insincere',4,1,'A politician makes an insincere promise. The speaker doubts the politician’s?','honesty of feeling or intention','ability to pronounce the word','knowledge of geography','这个评价质疑承诺者是否真心。')]});
D('insincerity',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 insincere 加名词后缀 -ity 构成，表示不真诚的状态；sincere 经法语源自拉丁语 sincerus‘纯正、真实’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insincerity"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"职场 · 信任","senseId":"insincerity.s1","en":"Repeated promises without action made the team's insincerity obvious, and staff stopped relying on the manager's public assurances.","zh":"一再承诺却没有行动，让团队显得毫无诚意；员工也不再相信经理公开作出的保证。","structure":"Repeated promises without action made the team's insincerity obvious / and staff stopped relying / on the manager's public assurances.","grammar":"insincerity 作 made 的宾语；make + 宾语 + 形容词表示使某事显得如何。","rationale":"言行不一致暴露出缺乏真诚，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The repeated insincerity in his public apologies weakened the audience’s trust.','他在公开道歉中一再表现出的虚伪削弱了听众的信任。')],mistakes:[m('Her insincerity was obvious because every statement was honest and heartfelt.','Her sincerity was obvious because every statement was honest and heartfelt.','诚实且发自内心说明 sincerity，而非 insincerity；去掉 in- 即可。')],quiz:[q('insincerity',1,1,'Insincerity in an apology means the apology?','is not genuinely felt','is followed by a repair','was delivered in a quiet room','insincerity 指情感或表达不真诚。'),q('insincerity',2,1,'A listener detects insincerity when praise seems?','false or merely convenient','completely heartfelt','unrelated to any speaker','虚假的赞扬会让人察觉 insincerity。'),q('insincerity',3,1,'Which noun is closest in meaning?','hypocrisy','honesty','kindness','hypocrisy 也表示虚伪。'),q('insincerity',4,1,'The suffix in insincerity turns the adjective insincere into?','a noun naming the quality','a verb describing an action','an adverb describing manner','-ity 构成表示性质的名词 insincerity。')]});
D('insinuate',{
    etymology: {"origin":"16世纪20年代来自拉丁语 insinuatus（insinuare 的过去分词），原指‘曲折地进入、迂回带入’，由 in-‘进入’与 sinuare‘弯曲、蜿蜒’构成；‘旁敲侧击暗示’义见于16世纪。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insinuate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"职场 · 委婉指责","senseId":"insinuate.s1","en":"Rather than accuse her colleague directly, he insinuated that someone had altered the figures, although he offered no evidence for the suggestion.","zh":"他没有直接指责同事，而是暗示有人改动了数字，尽管他没有为这种说法提供证据。","structure":"Rather than accuse her colleague directly / he insinuated that someone had altered the figures / although he offered no evidence for the suggestion.","grammar":"insinuate that + 从句表示含蓄地暗示；rather than 后接动词原形。","rationale":"说话者间接暗示同事有不当行为，吻合 s1 的负面暗示义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'By asking who had access to the files, the manager insinuated that someone had leaked them.','经理问谁能接触这些文件，暗示有人泄露了它们。')],mistakes:[m('He insinuated that the witness had lied, then clearly stated that he made no suggestion about the witness at all.','He insinuated that the witness had lied, though he did not state the accusation directly.','insinuate 本来就是间接暗示；说“完全没有暗示”与前句冲突，改成未直接明说。')],quiz:[q('insinuate',1,1,'“Are you insinuating that I cheated?” asks whether the speaker is?','hinting indirectly at an accusation','stating a proven fact in court','asking for directions to a school','insinuate 常指含蓄地暗示，尤其是负面含义。'),q('insinuate',2,1,'A colleague insinuates that a report was altered. The colleague?','suggests it indirectly rather than saying it openly','prints the report without reading it','proves who altered it beyond doubt','暗示不等于直接陈述或证明。'),q('insinuate',3,1,'Which clause fits the usual pattern? “She insinuated ___ the figures were false.”','that','on','to','常见结构是 insinuate that 从句。'),q('insinuate',4,1,'If a speaker insinuates wrongdoing, the suggestion is often?','unpleasant or damaging','a direct compliment','a neutral weather description','来源释义特别指出其常暗示不好的事。')]});
D('insist',{
    etymology: {"origin":"16世纪80年代经法语 insister 或直接来自拉丁语 insistere‘站在……上、坚持’，由 in-‘在上’与 sistere‘站立’构成；引申为坚决要求或坚持某说法。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insist"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"消费者 · 维权","senseId":"insist.s1","en":"When the damaged parcel arrived, Rosa insisted on a replacement and kept the delivery photographs in case the seller disputed her claim.","zh":"损坏的包裹送到后，罗莎坚决要求换货，并留存送货照片，以防卖家否认她的主张。","structure":"When the damaged parcel arrived / Rosa insisted on a replacement / and kept the delivery photographs in case the seller disputed her claim.","grammar":"insist on + 名词或 -ing 表示坚持要求；in case 引出预防某种情况。","rationale":"罗莎坚定要求采取换货措施，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The chair insisted on the importance of publishing the safety data.','主席强调了公布安全数据的重要性。')],mistakes:[m('He insisted me to sign the form before reading it.','He insisted that I sign the form before reading it.','insist 不直接用“insist somebody to do”；改为 insist that + 从句是本义项支持的结构。')],quiz:[q('insist',1,1,'She insisted on paying the bill. She?','firmly demanded that she pay','asked the waiter to cancel the bill','claimed that someone else had paid','insist on doing 表示坚持要做某事。'),q('insist',2,2,'He insisted that he had locked the door. He?','firmly maintained that the claim was true','asked someone to lock the door for him','admitted that he had left it open','insist that 可表示坚称某事属实。'),q('insist',3,3,'The report insists on the need for repairs. It?','strongly emphasizes that repairs are needed','offers repairs as an optional hobby','claims the building has already collapsed','insist on a point 可指强烈强调某事。'),q('insist',4,1,'Which sentence uses a standard pattern?','They insisted on staying.','They insisted us to stay.','They insisted for staying.','正确搭配为 insist on + 名词或动名词。')]});
D('insistent',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 insist 加形容词后缀 -ent 构成；insist 于16世纪80年代来自拉丁语 insistere‘坚持、施压’，该词形容要求坚定而反复。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insist"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"客服 · 需求","senseId":"insistent.s1","en":"The insistent caller asked for a clear answer three times, but the agent checked the account before promising that the fee would be removed.","zh":"这位坚持不懈的来电者三次要求明确答复，但客服人员先核查账户，才承诺会取消费用。","structure":"The insistent caller asked for a clear answer three times / but the agent checked the account / before promising that the fee would be removed.","grammar":"insistent 修饰 caller；before + -ing 表示承诺前先核查。","rationale":"来电者反复而坚定地提出要求，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The insistent ringing continued until someone answered the office phone.','办公室电话持续响个不停，直到有人接听。')],mistakes:[m("She was insistent to leave before the doors closed.","She was insistent on leaving before the doors closed.","The standard pattern is be insistent on + noun or gerund.")],quiz:[q('insistent',1,1,'An insistent request is made?','firmly and repeatedly','once by accident','without any clear purpose','insistent 表示坚持的、反复要求的。'),q('insistent',2,1,'An insistent ringing is one that?','continues and demands attention','stops immediately and is barely heard','happens only after the phone is removed','声音或要求持续不停也可用 insistent 描述。'),q('insistent',3,1,'Which preposition completes the phrase? “She was insistent ___ leaving.”','on','at to','from with','常用搭配为 be insistent on doing something。'),q('insistent',4,1,'Which person is being insistent?','a buyer who repeatedly asks for a refund','a buyer who accepts the first answer and asks nothing more','a buyer who has not made a request','坚持反复提出要求的人符合 insistent。')]});
D('insolvent',{
    etymology: {"origin":"18世纪来自法语 insolvent 或拉丁语 insolventem，字面与‘不能偿还’有关，由否定前缀 in- 与 solvent（有偿付能力的）构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insolvent"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"商业 · 清偿能力","senseId":"insolvent.s1","en":"The supplier became insolvent after losing its largest contract, leaving several smaller businesses waiting for refunds and unpaid deliveries.","zh":"供应商失去最大合同后资不抵债，几家小企业因此一直等不到退款和未付货物。","structure":"The supplier became insolvent after losing its largest contract / leaving several smaller businesses waiting / for refunds and unpaid deliveries.","grammar":"become insolvent 表示变得无力偿债；after + -ing 表示原因发生在前。","rationale":"供应商无法履行退款和交货的付款义务，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The supplier became insolvent after losing its largest contract and missing several debt payments.','失去最大合同并拖欠数笔债务后，这家供应商无力偿付了。')],mistakes:[m('The insolvent company paid every debt on time and had more cash than it could use.','The solvent company paid every debt on time and had more cash than it could use.','按时偿清所有债务且现金充裕与 insolvent（无力偿债）相反；改成 solvent。')],quiz:[q('insolvent',1,1,'A business is insolvent when it?','cannot pay the debts it owes','has no customers but no debts either','has paid all its bills ahead of schedule','insolvent 的定义是无力偿还债务。'),q('insolvent',2,1,'A firm goes insolvent after missing loan payments. It has become?','unable to meet its financial obligations','more profitable than before','a government regulator','go insolvent 表示陷入无力偿债状态。'),q('insolvent',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym.','bankrupt','wealthy','creditworthy','bankrupt 与 insolvent 都表示破产或无力偿债。'),q('insolvent',4,1,'Which evidence most directly supports calling a company insolvent?','it cannot meet debts as they fall due','it has changed its logo','it has hired a new accountant','判断 insolvent 要看偿付债务的能力。')]});
D('inspect',{
    etymology: {"origin":"16世纪初来自拉丁语 inspectare 或 inspicere‘向内看、仔细查看’，由 in-‘向内’与 specere‘看’构成；英语可指检查或官方视察。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inspect"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"公共设施 · 巡查","senseId":"inspect.s2","en":"The safety officer will inspect the bridge on Monday, documenting cracks and checking whether the temporary supports remain secure after the storm.","zh":"安全官员将在周一视察这座桥，记录裂缝，并检查临时支撑在风暴后是否仍然牢固。","structure":"The safety officer will inspect the bridge on Monday / documenting cracks / and checking whether the temporary supports remain secure after the storm.","grammar":"inspect + 地点表示官方检查或视察；documenting 与 checking 并列说明检查工作。","rationale":"安全官员以职务身份到现场核查，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'Before the parade, the colonel inspected the troops standing in formation.','阅兵前，上校检阅了列队的部队。')],mistakes:[m('The safety officer inspected the ladder without looking at or testing any part of it.','The safety officer inspected the ladder by looking at and testing its parts.','inspect 表示仔细检查；完全没有查看或测试不能称为检查。')],quiz:[q('inspect',1,1,'A mechanic inspects an engine before approving repairs. The mechanic?','examines it carefully for problems','installs a different vehicle','guarantees it without looking','sense 1 指仔细查看以发现问题。'),q('inspect',2,2,'Officials inspect a school after a safety complaint. They?','visit it officially to check its condition','teach every class in the school','write a novel about the school','sense 2 是官方视察或巡查。'),q('inspect',3,3,'A general inspected the troops. The general?','formally reviewed the soldiers','repaired each soldier’s equipment privately','asked the troops to inspect the general','来源还收录军队检阅这一专门用法。'),q('inspect',4,1,'Which object can naturally be inspected for damage?','a cracked bicycle helmet','an event that has not happened','a thought that was never expressed','inspect 常接待检查的实物或场所。')]});
D('inspection',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 inspect 加名词后缀 -ion 构成；inspect 源自拉丁语 inspicere‘向内看、仔细查看’，因此 inspection 指细致检查。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inspect"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"质量 · 验收","senseId":"inspection.s1","en":"A final inspection found a loose wire behind the control panel, preventing the machine from being approved before the repair was complete.","zh":"最终检查在控制面板后发现一根松动的电线，因此机器在修复完成前未获批准。","structure":"A final inspection found a loose wire behind the control panel / preventing the machine from being approved / before the repair was complete.","grammar":"inspection 指仔细检查；prevent A from being done 表示阻止某事发生。","rationale":"检查是对设备状况的仔细核查，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The landlord arranged an inspection before the new tenants moved in.','房东安排在新租户搬入前进行检查。')],mistakes:[m('The house passed inspection despite serious cracks that the inspector marked unsafe.','The house failed inspection despite serious cracks that the inspector marked unsafe.','检查员将严重裂缝标为不安全时，房屋不能通过检查；只需将 passed 改为 failed。')],quiz:[q('inspection',1,1,'A safety inspection is?','a careful check of conditions or equipment','a payment made to a landlord','a plan for building a new bridge','inspection 指仔细查看或检查。'),q('inspection',2,1,'The car passed its inspection. This means it?','was checked and met the required standard','was sold without being examined','was inspected by its new owner only after a crash','pass inspection 表示通过检查。'),q('inspection',3,1,'Which verb commonly goes with inspection?','carry out','fall asleep','take apart from','carry out an inspection 是开展检查。'),q('inspection',4,1,'A routine inspection can be scheduled even when?','no problem has yet been reported','the building has been removed','the inspector has no permission to enter','inspection 可以按计划例行进行，不一定已有故障。')]});
D('inspector',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 inspect 加施事后缀 -or 构成，指负责检查或官方核验的人；inspect 源自拉丁语 inspicere‘向内查看’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inspect"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"交通 · 执法","senseId":"inspector.s1","en":"The ticket inspector checked each passenger's pass near the station exit and explained where travelers could appeal an incorrect charge.","zh":"检票员在车站出口附近检查每位乘客的车票，并说明旅客可到哪里申诉错误收费。","structure":"The ticket inspector checked each passenger's pass / near the station exit / and explained where travelers could appeal an incorrect charge.","grammar":"inspector 指执行检查的人；where 引导 explained 的间接疑问内容。","rationale":"此人负责官方核验乘车凭证，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The building inspector asked to see the fire exits before approving the renovation.','建筑检查员在批准翻修前要求查看消防出口。')],mistakes:[m('The building inspector was appointed to check the exits and had no responsibility to inspect the exits.','The building inspector was appointed to check the exits and had responsibility to inspect the exits.','受命检查出口的人有检查职责；删去 no 即可消除矛盾。')],quiz:[q('inspector',1,1,'A food-safety inspector visits a restaurant to?','check whether it follows official standards','prepare every meal on the menu','buy the restaurant from its owner','inspector 指负责检查或视察的人。'),q('inspector',2,1,'The inspector sealed the shop after finding serious violations. The inspector was?','an official checking the premises','a customer who ordered lunch','the shop’s delivery driver','官方检查人员可因违规采取行动。'),q('inspector',3,1,'Which word names the person who conducts an inspection?','inspector','inspection','inspect','-or 构成表示执行检查者的名词 inspector。'),q('inspector',4,1,'A school inspector requests access to classrooms. The person is likely?','an official reviewing the school','a student applying for admission','a guest looking for the library','该职位以官方身份查看学校情况。')]});
D('inspire',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪中期经古法语 enspirer 来自拉丁语 inspirare‘吹入、向……呼气’，由 in-‘进入’与 spirare‘呼吸’构成；比喻义为激励或赋予灵感。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/inspire"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"设计 · 灵感","senseId":"inspire.s2","en":"A visit to the repair workshop inspired Lena with an idea for a chair that could be assembled without glue or specialist tools.","zh":"参观维修工坊后，莉娜获得了灵感，想到设计一把无需胶水或专业工具就能组装的椅子。","structure":"A visit to the repair workshop inspired Lena with an idea / for a chair that could be assembled / without glue or specialist tools.","grammar":"inspire sb. with an idea 表示给某人灵感；that 从句修饰 chair。","rationale":"参观引出了一个设计想法，符合 s2 的赋予灵感义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(4,'The old guide uses inspire to mean “draw air into the lungs.”','这本旧指南用 inspire 表示“将空气吸入肺部”。')],mistakes:[m("The novel inspired to the young writer to keep a journal.","The novel inspired the young writer to keep a journal.","Inspire takes the person as a direct object before an infinitive: inspire someone to do something.")],quiz:[q('inspire',1,1,'A coach inspires the team to keep training. The coach?','encourages the team to act','asks the team to forget the goal','orders the team to stop immediately','sense 1 指鼓舞或激励某人去做事。'),q('inspire',2,2,'A landscape inspired a poem. The landscape?','gave the poet an idea','criticized the poem after it was written','was copied from the poem','sense 2 指启发灵感或促成创作。'),q('inspire',3,3,'The abandoned building inspires fear. It?','causes people to feel fear','teaches people to breathe','proves that nobody is afraid','sense 3 表示引起某种情感或反应。'),q('inspire',4,4,'In an old medical text, inspire can mean?','breathe in','breathe out','speak without taking a breath','来源列出的旧义是吸气；现代常用义多为鼓舞或启发。')]});
D('instal',{
    etymology: {"origin":"来自古法语 installer 和中世纪拉丁语 installare，原指把人安置到席位或职位上；现代 install/英国拼写 instal 也表示设置设备使之可用。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/install"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"设备 · 设置","senseId":"instal.s1","en":"The technician will instal the new alarm beside the back door, then test its sensors while the owner watches from the hallway.","zh":"技术人员会在后门旁安装新警报器，然后在屋主从走廊观察时测试传感器。","structure":"The technician will instal the new alarm beside the back door / then test its sensors / while the owner watches from the hallway.","grammar":"instal + 设备表示安装；英国拼写 instal 与 install 是同一动词的拼写变体。","rationale":"警报器被固定设置到可使用的位置，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The board installed Mei as chair after the members voted.','成员投票后，董事会正式任命梅为主席。'),ex(2,'After arriving, he installed himself in the quietest chair by the window.','到达后，他在窗边最安静的椅子上安顿下来。')],mistakes:[m('They instal the new alarm, then call the monthly payment an installation.','They instal the new alarm, then call the monthly payment an instalment.','表示每月一期付款应为 instalment，不是 installation；只替换误用的名词。')],quiz:[q('instal',1,1,'The crew will instal new software on the office computers. They will?','put the software in place so it can be used','remove all the computers from the office','write instructions without adding the software','instal 的设备义是安装或设置。'),q('instal',2,2,'She installed herself beside the fireplace. She?','settled herself comfortably there','appointed herself as the fireplace','removed the fireplace from the room','instal 也可指使自己或他人安顿下来。'),q('instal',3,3,'The council installed a new director. It?','formally put the director into the position','uninstalled the director’s computer','asked the director to leave office','install somebody as 表示正式任命就职。'),q('instal',4,1,'Which statement about spelling is correct?','instal is a British variant of install','instal is never used in British English','instal is the noun meaning a monthly payment','instal 是 install 的英式拼写变体。')]});
D('instalment',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 instal/install 加名词后缀 -ment 构成；英语 instalment 常指分期付款的一期，或分段刊播作品中的一部分。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/installment"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"媒体 · 连载","senseId":"instalment.s2","en":"The latest instalment ends just as the detective discovers a second key, leaving readers to wait a week for the next chapter.","zh":"最新一期连载恰好在侦探发现第二把钥匙时结束，让读者还要再等一周才能看到下一章。","structure":"The latest instalment ends just as the detective discovers a second key / leaving readers to wait a week / for the next chapter.","grammar":"instalment 指分期发布作品的一部分；just as 表示恰在某事发生时。","rationale":"这是一部连载故事的一期，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The final instalment of the radio drama will air on Friday.','这部广播剧的最后一集将在周五播出。')],mistakes:[m('They paid the loan in twelve instalment, one each month.','They paid the loan in twelve instalments, one each month.','twelve 后的可数名词需用复数；给 instalment 加 s 即可。')],quiz:[q('instalment',1,1,'A monthly instalment is?','one regular payment in a series','the full debt erased without payment','a receipt showing no money changed hands','instalment 的一义是分期付款中的一期。'),q('instalment',2,2,'The next instalment of a serial appears tomorrow. It is?','the next part of a story or program','a monthly payment on a loan','a tool used to install software','连载或连续播出的作品的一部分也叫 instalment。'),q('instalment',3,1,'Which phrase describes paying over time?','pay in instalments','pay in instants','pay by inspectors','pay in instalments 表示分期付款。'),q('instalment',4,2,'A newspaper publishes a novel in instalments. Readers receive it?','in separate parts over time','only as a single unpublished file','as a series of loan payments','连载 instalments 是逐期刊出的各部分。')]});
D('instance',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪经古法语 instance 或直接来自拉丁语 instantia‘存在、紧迫、例证’，源自 instare‘站在其上、紧逼’，由 in- 与 stare‘站立’构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instance"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"科学 · 举例","senseId":"instance.s1","en":"One instance of the pattern appears in the coastal data, where rainfall rose after the winds shifted toward the valley.","zh":"这种模式的一个例子出现在沿海数据中：风向转向山谷后，降雨量随之上升。","structure":"One instance of the pattern appears in the coastal data / where rainfall rose / after the winds shifted toward the valley.","grammar":"an instance of + 现象表示一个具体例子；where 引导修饰 data 的从句。","rationale":"沿海数据中的一次具体情况用来展示模式，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The lawyer instanced two earlier cases in support of her argument.','律师举出两个早先的案例来支持她的论点。')],mistakes:[m('For instance, the report cites a case, but gives no example at all.','For instance, the report cites a case as an example.','for instance 用来举例；引用具体案例却说完全没有例子相互矛盾。')],quiz:[q('instance',1,1,'“For instance, one family saved rainwater” introduces?','a specific example','a final conclusion with no example','the cause of a machine failure','for instance 用于引出例子。'),q('instance',2,2,'This is the first instance of the error. It is?','the first occurrence of that error','a general rule that errors never happen','an example written by the inspector','sense 2 指某种情况的一次发生。'),q('instance',3,3,'The speaker instanced a recent case. The speaker?','cited it as an example','prevented it from happening','asked it to become a legal rule','动词 instance 指举例说明，较正式。'),q('instance',4,1,'Choose the standard phrase meaning “for example.”','for instance','in instant','by insides','for instance 是固定表达。')]});
D('instant',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪中期经古法语或直接来自拉丁语 instantem（instare‘紧逼、迫近’的现在分词），字面有‘迫近的’意味，后发展为立即发生或瞬间的。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instant"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"急救 · 应急","senseId":"instant.s2","en":"The device sends an instant alert when smoke enters the room, giving residents time to leave before the hallway fills with fumes.","zh":"烟雾进入房间时，设备会立即发出警报，让居民有时间在走廊充满烟雾前离开。","structure":"The device sends an instant alert when smoke enters the room / giving residents time to leave / before the hallway fills with fumes.","grammar":"instant 修饰 alert，表示立即发出的；when 与 before 引出触发和截止时间。","rationale":"警报在烟雾进入时立刻发生，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(5,'The instant the gate opened, the first visitors stepped inside.','大门一打开，第一批访客就走了进去。'),ex(3,'She stirred instant coffee into hot water before the meeting.','会前她把速溶咖啡搅进热水里。')],mistakes:[m("The alarm gave an instant of warning when smoke appeared.","The alarm gave an instant warning when smoke appeared.","Here instant modifies warning; the phrase an instant of warning changes the grammatical construction and does not fit this intended adjective use.")],quiz:[q('instant',1,1,'“In an instant, the lights went out” means they went out?','in a very short moment','after exactly one year','only after a long delay','名词 instant 指极短的片刻。'),q('instant',2,2,'An instant reply arrives?','immediately','after several months','only after repeated reminders','形容词 instant 可表示立即发生的。'),q('instant',3,3,'Instant noodles are noodles that?','can be prepared quickly','must be grown in a minute','cannot be cooked with hot water','instant 修饰食物时可指速食、速溶。'),q('instant',4,5,'“The instant the bell rang, class began” means?','as soon as the bell rang','long before the bell rang','only if the bell rang twice','the instant 可作连词，表示一……就……。')]});
D('instead',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由短语 in stead 构成，stead 是古英语 stede‘位置、地方’；instead 原义为‘取代、代替另一个位置上的东西’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instead"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"交通 · 替代方案","senseId":"instead.s1","en":"The main road was closed for repairs, so we took the riverside path instead and reached the village before the market opened.","zh":"主干道因维修封闭，所以我们改走河边小路，赶在集市开门前到达村庄。","structure":"The main road was closed for repairs / so we took the riverside path instead / and reached the village before the market opened.","grammar":"instead 置于句末，表示用河边小路代替主干道；so 连接原因和结果。","rationale":"一条路线取代另一条路线，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The bus was delayed, so we walked instead.','公交车晚点了，所以我们改为步行。')],mistakes:[m('She chose tea instead coffee because she wanted a drink in place of coffee.','She chose tea instead of coffee because she wanted a drink in place of coffee.','instead 不能直接接宾语；表示代替某物要用 instead of。')],quiz:[q('instead',1,1,'Use olive oil instead of butter. This means?','olive oil replaces the butter','olive oil is added only after the butter','neither oil nor butter is used','instead of 表示用一种东西代替另一种。'),q('instead',2,2,'He did not take a taxi; he walked instead. What happened?','walking replaced taking a taxi','he took both a taxi and a walk to work','he did not travel at all','句末 instead 表示改用另一种做法。'),q('instead',3,1,'Which sentence uses the preposition correctly?','We stayed home instead of going out.','We stayed home instead going out.','We stayed home instead to going out.','instead of 后可接名词或动名词。'),q('instead',4,2,'The meeting was not on Tuesday; it took place on Wednesday instead. Wednesday was?','the alternative day','an additional meeting day as well','the day before Tuesday','instead 在此表示改为另一选择。')]});
D('instead of',{
    etymology: {"origin":"instead of 是英语介词短语，沿用 instead（历史上 in stead，‘取代’）并接 of 引出被替代的人或事物。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instead"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"工作 · 替代","senseId":"instead of.s1","en":"Instead of cancelling the inspection, the team moved it to the covered depot and completed every safety check before the next shipment.","zh":"团队没有取消检查，而是把它移到有遮蔽的仓库，并在下一批货物发出前完成了所有安全检查。","structure":"Instead of cancelling the inspection / the team moved it to the covered depot / and completed every safety check before the next shipment.","grammar":"instead of + 名词或 -ing 表示代替某事；instead of cancelling 后接动名词。","rationale":"团队用移地点并完成检查来代替取消检查，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The museum closed the west entrance instead of the main entrance.','博物馆关闭的是西侧入口，而不是主入口。')],mistakes:[m('They took the train instead the bus, choosing one form of transport in place of the other.','They took the train instead of the bus, choosing one form of transport in place of the other.','表示代替某物时固定说 instead of；只补上缺少的 of。')],quiz:[q('instead of',1,1,'“Instead of tea, she ordered juice” means she ordered?','juice in place of tea','both tea and juice','tea after finishing the juice','instead of 表示用后者替代前者。'),q('instead of',2,1,'Which phrase correctly means “rather than walking”?','instead of walking','instead walking of','instead to walk of','instead of 后可以接动名词。'),q('instead of',3,1,'He called by phone instead of sending a letter. What did he do?','used a call as the alternative','sent a letter as well as calling','did neither of the two things','句中电话联系替代了寄信。'),q('instead of',4,1,'Choose the natural pattern.','instead of the old method','instead the old method of','instead from the old method','介词短语 instead of 后接名词短语。')]});
D('instinct',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪初经古法语或直接来自拉丁语 instinctus‘冲动、激励’，源自 instinguere‘推动、促使’，由 in- 与 stinguere‘刺、驱策’相关；自然行为义后来发展。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instinct"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"野外 · 直觉","senseId":"instinct.s2","en":"Her instinct told her to step back from the unstable ledge before she noticed the loose stones sliding toward her boots.","zh":"她的直觉让她在注意到松石滑向靴子之前就从不稳的崖边退开。","structure":"Her instinct told her to step back from the unstable ledge / before she noticed the loose stones / sliding toward her boots.","grammar":"instinct told sb. to do 表示直觉促使某人做某事；before 引导时间从句。","rationale":"她未经深思便感到危险并采取行动，符合 s2 的直觉义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'She has an instinct for design and quickly notices when a layout feels unbalanced.','她有设计天分，很快就能察觉版面何时失衡。')],mistakes:[m("Her instinct tell her to leave the unstable bridge.","Her instinct tells her to leave the unstable bridge.","The singular subject instinct takes the third-person singular verb tells.")],quiz:[q('instinct',1,1,'A newborn animal feeds by instinct. It acts from?','a natural tendency it is born with','a lesson taught by a written manual','a decision made after years of study','sense 1 指与生俱来的行为倾向。'),q('instinct',2,2,'Her instinct told her not to enter the dark room. This was?','a feeling or intuition without deliberate reasoning','a rule printed on the door','a talent for playing music','sense 2 是促使人不假思索行动的直觉。'),q('instinct',3,3,'An instinct for business is?','a natural talent for business','a legal document about a company','a habit of avoiding every business','sense 3 指对某事的天分或天然倾向。'),q('instinct',4,2,'Which phrase is natural for this meaning?','trust your instinct','trust your insides on','trust instinctive from','trust your instinct 是相信直觉的常用说法。')]});
D('instinctive',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 instinct 加形容词后缀 -ive 构成；instinct 源自拉丁语 instinctus‘冲动、自然推动’，形容未经有意识思考便发生的反应。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instinct"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"运动 · 反应","senseId":"instinctive.s1","en":"The goalkeeper made an instinctive dive toward the lower corner, blocking the shot before he had time to plan his movement.","zh":"守门员本能地扑向球门下角，在来得及规划动作之前就挡住了射门。","structure":"The goalkeeper made an instinctive dive toward the lower corner / blocking the shot / before he had time to plan his movement.","grammar":"instinctive 修饰 dive；before 表示动作发生在有意识规划之前。","rationale":"扑救动作未经过刻意思考，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her instinctive reaction was to catch the falling glass before it hit the floor.','她的本能反应是在玻璃杯落地前伸手接住它。')],mistakes:[m("He made an instinctive move to runs from the falling branch.","He made an instinctive move to run from the falling branch.","The infinitive marker to must be followed by the base form run.")],quiz:[q('instinctive',1,1,'An instinctive reaction happens?','without conscious thought','only after a long calculation','because of a written order','instinctive 意为本能的、不假思索的。'),q('instinctive',2,1,'A child pulls a hand away from a hot surface instinctively. The movement is?','automatic and natural','carefully rehearsed for years','a formal instruction','本能地缩手是自然、自动的反应。'),q('instinctive',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym for “an instinctive response.”','automatic','planned','artificial','automatic 表示自动发生，与本能反应接近。'),q('instinctive',4,1,'Which context best fits instinctive?','She ducked before she had time to think.','She compared three plans for an hour.','She followed a diagram step by step.','立即闪避、来不及思考体现 instinctive。')]});
D('institute',{
    etymology: {"origin":"动词14世纪初来自拉丁语 institutus（instituere 的过去分词），意为‘建立、安排、任命’，由 in- 与 statuere‘使站立、设立’构成；名词机构义见于19世纪。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/institute"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"科研 · 组织","senseId":"institute.s1","en":"The institute coordinates field studies across three universities and publishes its methods so other researchers can repeat the measurements.","zh":"这家研究所协调三所大学的实地研究，并公开其方法，供其他研究人员重复测量。","structure":"The institute coordinates field studies across three universities / and publishes its methods / so other researchers can repeat the measurements.","grammar":"institute 作研究机构名词；so 引导目的或结果从句。","rationale":"该组织以研究为宗旨开展工作，符合名词 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The institute trains engineers in renewable-energy systems.','这所学院为工程师提供可再生能源系统培训。'),ex(4,'The company instituted legal proceedings against the former contractor.','公司对前承包商提起了法律诉讼。')],mistakes:[m("Last year, the council institute a new safety policy.","Last year, the council instituted a new safety policy.","The past-time marker last year requires the past-tense verb instituted.")],quiz:[q('institute',1,1,'A research institute is?','an organization established for research or a special purpose','a monthly payment on a loan','a person who checks a building','sense 1 指研究院或特定目的机构。'),q('institute',2,2,'An institute of technology is a?','college or school focused on a subject','legal case filed against a school','set of classroom instructions','sense 2 指某专业的学院或学校。'),q('institute',3,3,'The government instituted a new rule. It?','started or put the rule into effect','removed every rule from the law','asked citizens to invent a new word','动词 institute 可指创立或开始实施制度。'),q('institute',4,4,'The firm instituted proceedings against its supplier. It?','started legal action','hired the supplier as a teacher','ended a case without filing it','institute proceedings 是提起法律程序。')]});
D('institution',{
    etymology: {"origin":"约1400年经古法语 institucion 来自拉丁语 institutionem，源自 instituere‘建立、安排、教导’；早期指建立行为，后发展为社会制度或组织。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/institution"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"社会 · 制度","senseId":"institution.s2","en":"The institution of public libraries changed access to books by giving residents a shared place to read, study, and borrow materials.","zh":"公共图书馆制度改变了人们获取书籍的方式，为居民提供了共同阅读、学习和借阅资料的场所。","structure":"The institution of public libraries changed access to books / by giving residents a shared place / to read, study, and borrow materials.","grammar":"the institution of + 制度表示一种社会制度；by + -ing 说明其作用方式。","rationale":"句中说的是确立的公共服务制度，不是某个机构建筑，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(5,'The institution of universal suffrage changed the country’s political system.','普选制度的建立改变了这个国家的政治体系。')],mistakes:[m('Marriage is a social institution, but it is not a custom, system, or established practice.','Marriage is a social institution and an established social practice.','作为社会制度的婚姻本身就是社会惯例或制度；删去否定转折并明示关系。')],quiz:[q('institution',1,1,'A financial institution is usually?','a large organization such as a bank','a single financial opinion','a payment made once a month','sense 1 指银行等大型机构。'),q('institution',2,2,'The institution of marriage refers to?','the established social system or custom of marriage','a building where wedding photographs are kept','one couple’s wedding invitation','sense 2 指社会或法律制度、惯例。'),q('institution',3,3,'“The pub is a local institution” may mean it is?','a familiar, long-established local feature','a newly opened and unknown building','a government office that issues laws','sense 3 可指为人熟知、历史悠久的事物。'),q('institution',4,4,'A mental institution is a place where people may be?','cared for or confined','taught to play a musical instrument','issued a loan payment','sense 4 指收容或照护人的机构。')]});
D('instruct',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪初来自拉丁语 instructus（instruere 的过去分词），instruere 原指‘安排、建造’，也发展出‘教导、告知’义；构词常分析为 in- + struere。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instruct"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"教育 · 技能教学","senseId":"instruct.s2","en":"The trainer instructed new staff in the safe use of the cutting machine, then watched each person complete a supervised practice run.","zh":"培训师教新员工安全使用切割机，随后观察每个人在监督下完成一次练习操作。","structure":"The trainer instructed new staff in the safe use of the cutting machine / then watched each person / complete a supervised practice run.","grammar":"instruct sb. in + 技能或学科表示教导某人；watch sb. do 后接动词原形。","rationale":"培训师教授一项技能，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(4,'The family instructed a solicitor to handle the property dispute.','这家人委托律师处理房产纠纷。')],mistakes:[m('The court instructed the clerk to file the document, but gave no order, teaching, or information.','The court instructed the clerk to file the document, giving a clear order.','instruct someone to do something 表示发出指示；称其没有任何指示与句子冲突。')],quiz:[q('instruct',1,1,'The guide instructed visitors to remain behind the line. The guide?','officially told them what to do','asked them to teach the guide','reported that the line had disappeared','sense 1 指指示或命令某人做事。'),q('instruct',2,2,'She instructs students in mathematics. She?','teaches them mathematics','orders them to leave school','asks them to hire a teacher','sense 2 指教授某门学科或技能。'),q('instruct',3,3,'The staff were instructed that the office would close early. They were?','officially informed of the change','taught to build an office','asked to close the office forever','sense 3 可表示正式通知或告知。'),q('instruct',4,4,'He instructed a solicitor before going to court. He?','hired or formally asked the lawyer to act for him','taught the lawyer how to read','ordered the court to close','法律语境下 instruct a solicitor 指委托律师。')]});
D('instruction',{
    etymology: {"origin":"约1400年来自古法语 instruction 或拉丁语 instructio，源自 instruere‘安排、准备、教导’；现代常指说明如何做某事的文字或口头指示。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instruction"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"设备 · 使用说明","senseId":"instruction.s1","en":"Read the instruction on the label before mixing the cleaner with water, because the wrong ratio can damage the painted surface.","zh":"把清洁剂与水混合前先阅读标签上的说明，因为比例不当会损坏漆面。","structure":"Read the instruction on the label / before mixing the cleaner with water / because the wrong ratio can damage the painted surface.","grammar":"instruction 指告诉人如何操作的说明；before + -ing 标记先后顺序。","rationale":"标签提供操作步骤，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The package includes instructions for assembling the shelf safely.','包装内附有安全组装架子的说明。')],mistakes:[m('The instruction explained each step, but the reader had no directions about what to do.','The instruction explained each step, giving the reader directions about what to do.','解释每个步骤正是给出做法说明；把否定的“没有”改为“给出”。')],quiz:[q('instruction',1,1,'The instructions say to turn the handle clockwise. They are?','directions explaining how to do something','a list of musical instruments','a receipt for a recent purchase','instruction 可指指导做法的说明或指示。'),q('instruction',2,1,'A teacher gives an instruction to open the book. The teacher gives?','a direction or order','a payment','an example of a legal document','instruction 也可指一条指令。'),q('instruction',3,1,'Which verb naturally collocates with instruction?','follow','install into','insulate from','follow instructions 是常用搭配。'),q('instruction',4,1,'“Read the instruction before using the device” advises the user to?','check the directions first','ignore all operating information','take the device apart immediately','说明书可告诉使用者如何操作。')]});
D('instructions',{
    etymology: {"origin":"instructions 是 instruction 的复数形式；instruction 经古法语或拉丁语而来，源自 instruere‘准备、教导’，复数常指一组操作步骤。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instruction"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"维修 · 步骤","senseId":"instructions.s1","en":"The instructions say to unplug the lamp before opening its base, and they include a diagram showing where each small screw belongs.","zh":"说明书要求打开灯座前先拔掉插头，并附有示意图标出每颗小螺丝的位置。","structure":"The instructions say to unplug the lamp before opening its base / and they include a diagram / showing where each small screw belongs.","grammar":"instructions 作复数主语；say to do 表示说明要做什么；where 引导间接疑问。","rationale":"这组步骤指导用户如何操作，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Keep the instructions with the appliance in case it needs repair.','把说明书和电器放在一起，以备维修时查阅。')],mistakes:[m('The instructions explained how to assemble the desk, but contained no steps or directions.','The instructions explained how to assemble the desk and contained useful steps.','解释装配方法就包含步骤或指示；“没有步骤”与前半句矛盾。')],quiz:[q('instructions',1,1,'A set of instructions tells you?','the steps for doing or assembling something','the names of everyone who bought it','how much the package weighs','instructions 是说明步骤的内容。'),q('instructions',2,1,'If the instructions are missing, a user may lack?','directions for operating the product','the product’s physical parts','a list of shop opening hours','缺少说明书会使使用者没有操作指引。'),q('instructions',3,1,'Which verb fits the common phrase?','follow the instructions','wear the instructions','borrow the instructions into','follow instructions 表示按说明操作。'),q('instructions',4,1,'“Read the instructions carefully” is advice to?','check the directions before acting','ignore the directions and guess','replace the instructions with a receipt','instructions 是复数名词，指操作说明。')]});
D('instructor',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 instruct 加施事后缀 -or 构成，指教授技能或课程的人；instruct 源自拉丁语 instruere‘教导、安排’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instruct"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"培训 · 现场教学","senseId":"instructor.s1","en":"The climbing instructor checked every harness before showing the beginners how to tie a secure knot on the practice wall.","zh":"攀岩教练先检查了每条安全带，再向初学者演示如何在练习墙上系牢固的绳结。","structure":"The climbing instructor checked every harness / before showing the beginners / how to tie a secure knot on the practice wall.","grammar":"instructor 指教授技能的人；show sb. how to do 表示演示做法。","rationale":"此人向初学者教授攀岩技能，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The ski instructor demonstrated how to stop safely on a steep slope.','滑雪教练示范了如何在陡坡上安全停下。')],mistakes:[m("The instructor instructed to the trainees how to operate the lift.","The instructor instructed the trainees how to operate the lift.","Instruct takes a direct object for the learner; it is not instructed to someone in this construction.")],quiz:[q('instructor',1,1,'A driving instructor helps learners?','learn how to drive','inspect the road as a government official','write the car’s instruction manual','instructor 指教授某种技能的人。'),q('instructor',2,1,'A swimming instructor is most likely to?','teach people swimming skills','repair the swimming pool','sell tickets at the entrance','泳教教练的工作是教授游泳。'),q('instructor',3,1,'Which person is an instructor?','a teacher leading a practical lesson','a student taking the lesson','a person who only sells the classroom','instructor 是授课者或教练，不是学员。'),q('instructor',4,1,'The instructor demonstrated a technique before practice. The instructor?','showed students how to perform it','asked students to hire a lawyer','conducted a building inspection','示范技能是教练或授课者的行为。')]});
D('instrument',{
    etymology: {"origin":"13世纪末经古法语 instrument 来自拉丁语 instrumentum‘工具、器械、手段、文书’，源自 instruere‘安排、建造、教导’，由 in- 与 struere‘堆建’构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/instrument"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"社会 · 达成目标","senseId":"instrument.s3","en":"The grant became an instrument for restoring the wetland, funding local surveys and giving residents a formal role in monitoring water quality.","zh":"这笔拨款成为修复湿地的手段，为当地调查提供经费，也让居民正式参与水质监测。","structure":"The grant became an instrument for restoring the wetland / funding local surveys / and giving residents a formal role in monitoring water quality.","grammar":"an instrument for + -ing 表示实现目标的手段；funding 与 giving 并列说明作用。","rationale":"拨款被用来达成湿地修复目标，符合 s3 的手段义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(4,'The parties signed the legal instrument before the agreement took effect.','协议生效前，双方签署了这份法律文书。'),ex(5,'The composer instrumented the short theme for flute and strings.','作曲家为这段短主题编配了长笛和弦乐。')],mistakes:[m('The composer instrumented the piece for strings but arranged it for no instruments at all.','The composer instrumented the piece for strings and arranged it for string instruments.','为弦乐编配与完全不使用乐器相矛盾；删除否定并明确配器。')],quiz:[q('instrument',1,1,'A precision instrument in a laboratory is?','a tool or device used for a task','a musician who plays the piano','a set of legal rules','sense 1 指工具、设备或科学仪器。'),q('instrument',2,2,'She plays a wind instrument in the band. It is?','an object used to make music','a scientific measurement','a contract signed in court','sense 2 指乐器。'),q('instrument',3,3,'“Language is an instrument of thought” means language is?','a means used to achieve or support thought','a physical musical device','a signed legal document','sense 3 比喻指达到目的的手段或工具。'),q('instrument',4,4,'A legal instrument is?','a formal document','a violin used in a courtroom','a person who examines a building','sense 4 指正式法律文件。')]});
D('insufficient',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由否定前缀 in- 加 sufficient 构成；sufficient 经法语来自拉丁语 sufficiens（sufficere‘足以、供应’的现在分词），表示不足以满足所需。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insufficient"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"公共服务 · 供给","senseId":"insufficient.s1","en":"The emergency water supply was insufficient for the whole shelter, so volunteers arranged a second delivery before the evening meal.","zh":"应急供水不足以满足整个避难所的需求，因此志愿者在晚餐前安排了第二次送水。","structure":"The emergency water supply was insufficient for the whole shelter / so volunteers arranged a second delivery / before the evening meal.","grammar":"be insufficient for 表示对某用途不足；so 引出因此采取的措施。","rationale":"供水量达不到避难所的需要，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The evidence was insufficient to identify the source of the leak.','这些证据不足以确定泄漏源头。')],mistakes:[m('The evidence was insufficient, yet it fully proved every detail beyond doubt.','The evidence was sufficient, and it fully proved every detail beyond doubt.','“证据不足”与“充分证明每个细节”相冲突；改为 sufficient。')],quiz:[q('insufficient',1,1,'Insufficient evidence is evidence that?','is not enough for the purpose','proves every claim conclusively','has been collected in excessive amounts','insufficient 表示数量或程度不够。'),q('insufficient',2,1,'The fund was insufficient to repair the bridge. The fund?','did not contain enough money for the repair','was larger than the repair could use','had already repaired the bridge','资金不足以完成维修。'),q('insufficient',3,1,'Choose the closest opposite of insufficient.','adequate','scarce','deficient','adequate 表示足够、适当。'),q('insufficient',4,1,'Which phrase is natural?','insufficient time to finish','insufficient of time for finish','time insufficiently of finishing','insufficient 可直接修饰名词 time。')]});
D('insulate',{
    etymology: {"origin":"16世纪初经法语 isoler 的相关形式或由 Latin insulatus ‘使成岛状’而来，关联 insula‘岛’；现代义指用材料隔热、隔音或保护免受影响。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insulate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"建筑 · 节能","senseId":"insulate.s1","en":"The owners insulated the attic with recycled fiber, reducing heat loss in winter without covering the vents needed for safe airflow.","zh":"房主用再生纤维给阁楼做了隔热处理，减少冬季热量流失，同时没有堵住安全通风所需的风口。","structure":"The owners insulated the attic with recycled fiber / reducing heat loss in winter / without covering the vents needed for safe airflow.","grammar":"insulate A with B 表示用 B 给 A 做隔热；reducing 分词说明效果。","rationale":"材料减少热量传出，符合 s1 的隔热义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'Rubber gloves insulate the technician from electric current.','橡胶手套使技术人员与电流绝缘。'),ex(3,'The family insulated the child from constant online criticism.','家人使孩子免受持续不断的网络批评。')],mistakes:[m('The exposed wire was insulated with bare metal that let current pass freely.','The exposed wire was left uninsulated with bare metal that let current pass freely.','裸露金属允许电流通过，不能据此称导线已绝缘；加 un- 可表达未绝缘。')],quiz:[q('insulate',1,1,'Insulating a roof helps?','reduce the passage of heat or sound','make the roof leak more easily','turn the roof into a musical instrument','sense 1 是隔热或隔音。'),q('insulate',2,2,'A plastic coating can insulate a wire by?','preventing electric current from escaping','making the wire conduct more strongly','using the wire as a legal document','sense 2 指给导线包覆绝缘层。'),q('insulate',3,3,'A manager may insulate a team from criticism by?','protecting it from that unpleasant experience','making the criticism louder','asking the team to criticize itself','sense 3 比喻指保护某人免受不良影响。'),q('insulate',4,1,'Which phrase has the usual meaning?','insulate a wall against heat','insulate a wall into criticism','insulate a wall to a wire','insulate 常接被隔热或隔音的对象。')]});
D('insulated',{
    etymology: {"origin":"insulated 是 insulate 的过去分词形容词；insulate 与拉丁语 insula‘岛’相关，原有‘隔开’的构词联想，现代可指隔绝热或声音。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insulate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"住宅 · 保温","senseId":"insulated.s1","en":"The insulated water pipes stayed above freezing during the cold night, while the exposed section near the gate began to form ice.","zh":"寒夜里，做好隔热的水管仍保持在冰点以上，而大门旁裸露的管段开始结冰。","structure":"The insulated water pipes stayed above freezing during the cold night / while the exposed section near the gate / began to form ice.","grammar":"insulated 修饰 water pipes；while 对照保温与裸露两种状态。","rationale":"水管的热量不易散失，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The insulated walls kept the bedroom warm through the winter.','隔热的墙壁让卧室整个冬天都保持温暖。')],mistakes:[m('The insulated pipe lost heat rapidly because it had no protective covering.','The uninsulated pipe lost heat rapidly because it had no protective covering.','没有保护层且迅速散热说明管道未隔热；改为 uninsulated。')],quiz:[q('insulated',1,1,'An insulated wall is?','protected against the passage of heat or sound','open to every draft and temperature change','built only from musical instruments','insulated 表示经过隔热、隔音等处理的。'),q('insulated',2,1,'An insulated wire is safer because its coating?','helps prevent electric current from escaping','makes the wire carry no signal ever','acts as a monthly payment','绝缘层用于阻止电流外泄。'),q('insulated',3,1,'Which object could be insulated to keep drinks cold?','a cooler box','a paper receipt','a loudspeaker with no casing','隔热材料可减缓冷藏箱内外的热交换。'),q('insulated',4,1,'The room was well insulated, so it?','kept heat from passing through the walls easily','lost all warmth immediately','had no walls at all','well insulated 表示隔热效果良好。')]});
D('insult',{
    etymology: {"origin":"动词16世纪60年代经法语 insulter 或直接来自拉丁语 insultare‘扑向、攻击’，由 in-‘向上/向着’与 salire‘跳’构成；言语冒犯义见于17世纪初。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insult"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"职场 · 尊重","senseId":"insult.s1","en":"Calling a colleague incompetent in front of the whole team would insult her, even if the speaker later claimed that the comment was only a joke.","zh":"在整个团队面前称同事无能会冒犯她，即使说话者后来声称那只是个玩笑。","structure":"Calling a colleague incompetent in front of the whole team would insult her / even if the speaker later claimed / that the comment was only a joke.","grammar":"insult + 人表示侮辱某人；动名词短语作主语，even if 引导让步从句。","rationale":"公开贬低同事构成不尊重的言语冒犯，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The critic called the sculpture an insult to the eye, not merely an awkward design.','评论家称这座雕塑简直伤害眼睛，而不只是设计笨拙。')],mistakes:[m('Calling her careful work “useless” was an insult, but it was a respectful compliment.','Calling her careful work “useless” was an insult, but it was not a respectful compliment.','把工作称为无用是冒犯，不可能同时是尊重的赞美；补上 not。')],quiz:[q('insult',1,1,'To insult a colleague is to?','speak or act rudely toward them','offer them sincere thanks','inspect their work carefully','sense 1 是以粗鲁冒犯的方式对人。'),q('insult',2,2,'“That remark was an insult” means the remark was?','rude or offensive','a formal legal document','a friendly instruction','名词 insult 可指侮辱性言行。'),q('insult',3,3,'Calling a beautiful building “an insult to the eye” means it?','is extremely ugly or offensive to look at','has injured someone’s eyesight physically','is an official eye examination','sense 3 是对视觉美感的比喻性伤害。'),q('insult',4,1,'The noun and verb differ in stress: the noun is stressed?','on the first syllable','only on the last syllable','equally on every syllable','名词 insult 重音在前，动词 insult 重音在后。')]});
D('insulting',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 insult 的现在分词形式转作形容词，约1590年代已有记录，表示含有侮辱或冒犯意味；insult 源自拉丁语 insultare‘扑向、攻击’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insult"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"沟通 · 措辞","senseId":"insulting.s1","en":"The email sounded insulting because it blamed the receptionist for a system failure that she had neither caused nor been told about.","zh":"这封邮件听起来带有侮辱性，因为它把系统故障归咎于既未造成故障、也未被告知情况的接待员。","structure":"The email sounded insulting / because it blamed the receptionist for a system failure / that she had neither caused nor been told about.","grammar":"sound insulting 表示听起来冒犯；neither…nor…并列两个否定情况。","rationale":"邮件措辞贬低并不公正地责怪对方，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The judge rejected the insulting remark and asked counsel to rephrase it.','法官驳回了这句侮辱性言论，并要求律师重新措辞。')],mistakes:[m('He made an insulting comment that praised her work respectfully and caused no offense.','He made an appreciative comment that praised her work respectfully and caused no offense.','尊重地赞扬且不冒犯的话与 insulting（侮辱性的）相反；改为 appreciative。')],quiz:[q('insulting',1,1,'An insulting comment is likely to?','offend or belittle someone','offer genuine praise','give neutral directions','insulting 表示带有侮辱或冒犯意味的。'),q('insulting',2,1,'Which response would be insulting?','mocking someone’s accent in front of others','thanking someone for their help','asking politely for clarification','嘲笑口音会使对方感到受辱。'),q('insulting',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym.','offensive','respectful','grateful','offensive 与 insulting 意思接近。'),q('insulting',4,1,'The tone sounded insulting, so the listener felt?','disrespected','encouraged to relax','certain the speaker was praising them','侮辱性的语气会让人感到不受尊重。')]});
D('insurance',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 insure 加名词后缀 -ance 构成；insure 与 assure 相关，均经法语或拉丁语 assurare 等形式进入英语，现代 insurance 指为风险提供财务保障的安排。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insurance"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"出行 · 风险保障","senseId":"insurance.s1","en":"Their travel insurance covered emergency medical care abroad, but the couple read the exclusions carefully before paying for the more expensive plan.","zh":"他们的旅行保险涵盖海外紧急医疗，但这对夫妇在购买更贵的方案前仔细阅读了除外条款。","structure":"Their travel insurance covered emergency medical care abroad / but the couple read the exclusions carefully / before paying for the more expensive plan.","grammar":"insurance 作不可数名词，指风险保障；cover 在此表示保险涵盖某费用。","rationale":"保险方案在符合条件时承担费用，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Before renting the car, we checked that our travel insurance covered collision damage.','租车前，我们确认旅行保险涵盖碰撞损坏。')],mistakes:[m("They bought an insurance for the trip.","They bought insurance for the trip.","Insurance meaning financial protection is normally uncountable in this construction, so it takes no an.")],quiz:[q('insurance',1,1,'Travel insurance is bought to?','provide financial protection against certain losses','guarantee that no accident can happen','replace a passport at the airport','insurance 提供约定风险发生时的经济保障。'),q('insurance',2,1,'A person buys insurance and pays?','a premium for coverage under a policy','a fine for breaking a law','the full cost of every future accident','保险通常按保单支付保费以获得保障。'),q('insurance',3,1,'Which phrase uses the uncountable noun naturally?','buy insurance','buy an insurance for the trip','buy many insurance','该来源把 insurance 收为不可数名词，常说 buy insurance。'),q('insurance',4,1,'Insurance coverage can help with?','the financial cost of a covered event','the certainty that every event is harmless','the removal of all legal responsibilities','保险补偿取决于保单涵盖的事件。')]});
D('insurgent',{
    etymology: {"origin":"来自拉丁语 insurgentem（insurgere‘起身、起而反抗’的现在分词），由 in- 与 surgere‘升起’构成；英语名词指反抗统治者或政府的人。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insurgent"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"历史 · 冲突","senseId":"insurgent.s1","en":"The insurgent group announced a ceasefire, but aid workers waited for independent confirmation before sending medical supplies through the mountain pass.","zh":"叛乱组织宣布停火，但援助人员等待独立确认后，才通过山口运送医疗物资。","structure":"The insurgent group announced a ceasefire / but aid workers waited for independent confirmation / before sending medical supplies through the mountain pass.","grammar":"insurgent 修饰 group，表示叛乱者组成的团体；before + -ing 表示运输前先确认。","rationale":"该团体反抗现有统治当局，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The insurgent group demanded political changes and rejected the government’s authority.','叛乱团体要求政治变革，并拒绝承认政府权威。')],mistakes:[m('The insurgents defended the rulers against rebellion and fought to preserve the government’s control.','The government forces defended the rulers against rebellion and fought to preserve the government’s control.','insurgents 是反抗统治者的叛乱者，不是保卫统治者的一方；改为 government forces。')],quiz:[q('insurgent',1,1,'An insurgent is someone who?','fights against an established authority','works as an official tax inspector','writes instructions for new employees','insurgent 指反抗统治者或当局的人。'),q('insurgent',2,1,'Insurgent forces seized a town. These forces were?','rebels fighting the ruling government','the government’s routine school inspectors','a group of visiting musicians','insurgent 可作形容词修饰叛乱武装。'),q('insurgent',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym.','rebel','minister','instructor','rebel 与 insurgent 都指叛乱者。'),q('insurgent',4,1,'The label insurgent is most closely linked with?','an armed or political uprising against rulers','a peaceful class lesson','a routine financial inspection','词义与政治叛乱相关。')]});
D('insurrection',{
    etymology: {"origin":"来自拉丁语 insurrectionem（insurrectio 的宾格），源自 insurgere‘起身、起而反抗’，由 in- 与 surgere‘升起’构成；名词指反抗统治者的起义。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/insurrection"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"历史 · 政治变局","senseId":"insurrection.s1","en":"The failed insurrection left the capital under strict curfew, while negotiators tried to prevent further violence between government forces and civilians.","zh":"起义失败后，首都实施严格宵禁；谈判人员则努力防止政府军与平民之间发生更多暴力。","structure":"The failed insurrection left the capital under strict curfew / while negotiators tried to prevent further violence / between government forces and civilians.","grammar":"insurrection 作主语，指反抗统治者的武装起事；leave + 宾语 + 状态补语。","rationale":"事件是反抗政府的起义，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The failed insurrection left the capital under strict military control.','起义失败后，首都处于严格的军事管控之下。')],mistakes:[m('The insurrection supported the rulers and ended the rebellion without opposing them.','The government’s suppression of the insurrection supported the rulers and ended the rebellion.','insurrection 本身是反抗统治者的起义，支持统治者的是镇压起义的行动。')],quiz:[q('insurrection',1,1,'An insurrection is?','an organized rising against rulers','a routine election campaign','a small payment made every month','insurrection 指反抗统治者的起义。'),q('insurrection',2,1,'A report says the insurrection failed. The uprising?','did not succeed','was a peaceful school inspection','successfully ended in a new ruler’s appointment','起义失败表示未实现目标。'),q('insurrection',3,1,'Which word is a close synonym?','uprising','instruction','insurance','uprising 与 insurrection 都表示起义。'),q('insurrection',4,1,'A government may try to suppress an insurrection by?','using force to stop the revolt','publishing installments of a novel','inspecting a school kitchen','镇压起义是对叛乱行动的反制。')]});
D('intact',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪初来自拉丁语 intactus‘未触碰、未受损’，由否定前缀 in- 与 tactus（tangere‘触摸’的过去分词）构成。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intact"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"救援 · 物品状况","senseId":"intact.s1","en":"Rescuers found the sealed medicine box intact beneath the fallen shelf, so they checked its temperature record before using anything inside.","zh":"救援人员在倒下的架子下发现密封药箱完好无损，因此在使用里面的药品前先检查了温度记录。","structure":"Rescuers found the sealed medicine box intact beneath the fallen shelf / so they checked its temperature record / before using anything inside.","grammar":"find + 宾语 + intact 表示发现某物仍完好；before + -ing 标示使用前的检查。","rationale":"药箱没有破损，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The editor kept the original wording intact while correcting the page layout.','编辑在修正页面版式时保留了原文措辞。')],mistakes:[m('The vase arrived intact, with its handle broken into three pieces.','The vase arrived damaged, with its handle broken into three pieces.','把手碎成三块说明花瓶受损，不能称 intact；改为 damaged。')],quiz:[q('intact',1,1,'A vase that survived a fall intact is?','whole and undamaged','missing several pieces','completely redesigned','sense 1 指完好无损、未受损伤。'),q('intact',2,2,'The original text remained intact after editing. It was?','kept complete and unchanged','rewritten with several sections removed','translated into a different language','sense 2 指内容完整、未被改动。'),q('intact',3,1,'Which phrase is natural?','remain intact','break intact','intact into pieces','remain intact 表示继续保持完整。'),q('intact',4,1,'A document left intact has?','not been altered or had parts removed','been edited beyond recognition','been destroyed before anyone read it','intact 可形容完整保存、未经改动的材料。')]});
D('intake',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 in + take 形成，字面指‘取入、吸入’；英语名词可指摄入的数量、被接收的一批人，或供空气、水、燃料进入的开口。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intake"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"健康 · 饮食","senseId":"intake.s1","en":"The dietitian asked Sam to record his daily water intake for a week, including drinks at work and the glass he had before bed.","zh":"营养师让萨姆连续一周记录每日饮水量，包括工作时喝的饮料和睡前那杯水。","structure":"The dietitian asked Sam to record his daily water intake for a week / including drinks at work / and the glass he had before bed.","grammar":"water intake 表示摄入的水量；ask sb. to do 后接不定式。","rationale":"记录的是摄入的数量，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The new intake of nursing students begins clinical practice in September.','新招收的护理学生将在九月开始临床实习。'),ex(3,'Dust blocked the engine’s air intake and reduced its power.','灰尘堵塞了发动机进气口，导致功率下降。')],mistakes:[m("The college accepted intake of 120 new students that year.","The college accepted an intake of 120 new students that year.","Intake is a singular count noun here and needs the article an.")],quiz:[q('intake',1,1,'A doctor asks a patient to reduce salt intake. The patient should reduce?','the amount of salt consumed','the number of students admitted','the opening that lets air into an engine','sense 1 指食物、饮料或空气的摄入量。'),q('intake',2,2,'A college has an intake of 400 this year. It has?','accepted a group of 400 students','used 400 air filters','received 400 separate loan payments','sense 2 指学校新招收的人数或群体。'),q('intake',3,3,'An engine’s air intake is?','an opening through which air enters','a total measure of salt eaten','a group of new employees','sense 3 指空气、燃料等进入的开口。'),q('intake',4,1,'Which collocation refers to food consumed?','daily calorie intake','daily inspector intake','daily instruction intake','calorie intake 是热量摄入量。')]});
D('intangible',{
    etymology: {"origin":"16世纪来自中世纪拉丁语 intangibilis，由否定前缀 in- 与 tangibilis‘可触摸的’构成；后者源自 tangere‘触摸’，表示无实体、不能触摸。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intangible"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"文化 · 价值","senseId":"intangible.s1","en":"The archive preserves intangible heritage such as songs and oral histories, which cannot be stored as objects but still shape the community's identity.","zh":"档案馆保存着歌曲和口述历史等非物质遗产；它们不能作为实物存放，却仍塑造着社群身份。","structure":"The archive preserves intangible heritage such as songs and oral histories / which cannot be stored as objects / but still shape the community's identity.","grammar":"intangible 修饰 heritage，表示没有可触摸的实体形态；which 引导定语从句。","rationale":"歌曲和口述传统没有实体形状但具有文化价值，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'There is an intangible warmth in the little bookshop that is hard to describe.','这家小书店有一种难以言说的温馨感。'),ex(3,'The brand’s reputation is an intangible that attracts loyal customers.','这个品牌的声誉是一种吸引忠实顾客的无形资产。')],mistakes:[m('The company listed its intangible assets as office desks and delivery vans that could be touched.','The company listed its tangible assets as office desks and delivery vans that could be touched.','桌椅和货车都是可触摸的实体，不是 intangible assets；改为 tangible。')],quiz:[q('intangible',1,1,'An intangible asset has?','value but no physical form you can touch','a solid shape that can be lifted','no value to its owner','sense 1 指没有可触摸实体的无形事物。'),q('intangible',2,2,'An intangible charm is difficult to?','describe or measure precisely','touch with a finger','weigh on a scale','sense 2 表示难以准确描述或衡量的特质。'),q('intangible',3,3,'Trust is one of a company’s intangibles. It is?','a valuable nonphysical asset','a machine stored in a warehouse','a cash payment made every month','sense 3 可作名词，指有价值的无形资产。'),q('intangible',4,1,'Which phrase is common in business?','intangible assets','intangible bricks','intangible kilograms','intangible assets 是常见经济学搭配。')]});
D('integral',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪中期经法语或直接来自拉丁语 integralis，源自 integer‘完整的、整体的’；英语常用 integral 表示构成整体所必需的部分。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/integral"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"工程 · 系统","senseId":"integral.s1","en":"Clear labeling is integral to the emergency plan, because responders must identify each valve quickly when power and communications fail.","zh":"清晰的标签是应急方案不可或缺的一部分，因为电力和通信失灵时，救援人员必须迅速辨认每个阀门。","structure":"Clear labeling is integral to the emergency plan / because responders must identify each valve quickly / when power and communications fail.","grammar":"be integral to 表示对整体必不可少；because 引出其必要性。","rationale":"没有清晰标记，关键应急流程难以执行，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'In calculus, the integral gives a quantity accumulated over an interval.','在微积分中，积分给出某个区间上累积的量。')],mistakes:[m('The seal was an integral part of the vessel, but the vessel was complete without the seal.','The seal was an integral part of the vessel, but the vessel was incomplete without the seal.','不可或缺的部件缺失会使整体不完整；只需补上 incomplete 中的 in-。')],quiz:[q('integral',1,1,'A reliable power supply is integral to the hospital. It is?','necessary for the hospital to function','a decorative feature the hospital can easily lose','a service unrelated to the hospital','sense 1 的 integral to 表示对整体必不可少。'),q('integral',2,2,'An integral design includes?','all the parts that belong together as a whole','only one isolated part','a missing section that was never planned','sense 2 强调整体或应有部分完整。'),q('integral',3,3,'In mathematics, an integral may be?','a result of integrating a function','a decimal fraction only','a type of musical instrument','sense 3 是数学术语“积分”；来源也列整数义。'),q('integral',4,1,'Which construction is standard?','an integral part of the plan','an integral part to the plan','an integral of the plan part','常说 an integral part of something。')]});
D('integrate',{
    etymology: {"origin":"17世纪30年代来自拉丁语 integratus（integrare 的过去分词），意为‘使完整’；integrare 源自 integer‘完整的’，英语后来发展出把人融入群体的用法。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/integrate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"社区 · 融入","senseId":"integrate.s2","en":"The language program pairs new arrivals with local volunteers so they can integrate into neighborhood life while keeping ties to their own traditions.","zh":"语言项目把新移民与当地志愿者配对，让他们在保留自身传统联系的同时融入社区生活。","structure":"The language program pairs new arrivals with local volunteers / so they can integrate into neighborhood life / while keeping ties to their own traditions.","grammar":"integrate into + 群体或社会表示融入；while + -ing 表示同时保留另一状态。","rationale":"新移民逐渐成为社区生活的一部分，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The new arrivals integrated into the neighborhood through a local sports club.','新来者通过当地体育俱乐部融入了社区。'),ex(3,'The class integrated the function over the stated interval.','全班对给定区间上的函数进行了积分。')],mistakes:[m('The new software integrated the payment and inventory tools into one system but kept them entirely separate.','The new software integrated the payment and inventory tools into one system and combined them.','integrate A into one system 表示把它们整合起来；“完全分开”与此相反。')],quiz:[q('integrate',1,1,'The company integrated two databases into one platform. It?','combined them so they worked as one system','deleted both databases without replacement','copied each database into a separate office','sense 1 指合并不同事物使其成为一个系统。'),q('integrate',2,2,'A student integrated into a new community. The student?','became part of the group','created a new mathematical function','remained entirely outside the group','sense 2 指融入群体或社会。'),q('integrate',3,3,'In a calculus problem, “integrate the function” means?','find its integral','split it into unrelated words','measure the function’s color','数学动词 integrate 表示求积分。'),q('integrate',4,1,'Which pattern is natural?','integrate the tool into the system','integrate the tool at the system','integrate the tool for to system','常见结构是 integrate A into B。')]});
D('integrated',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 integrate 的过去分词转作形容词，意为各部分已结合成一个整体；integrate 源自拉丁语 integrare‘使完整’，来自 integer‘完整的’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/integrate"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"教育 · 课程设计","senseId":"integrated.s1","en":"The integrated course links history, science, and writing through one local river project, so students use evidence from several subjects together.","zh":"这门综合课程通过一个本地河流项目把历史、科学和写作联系起来，让学生综合运用多个学科的证据。","structure":"The integrated course links history, science, and writing through one local river project / so students use evidence / from several subjects together.","grammar":"integrated 修饰 course，表示不同部分组合在一起；link A, B, and C 连接多个领域。","rationale":"多门学科围绕同一项目结合成一个整体，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The clinic offers an integrated service that combines medical care and counseling.','这家诊所提供整合医疗服务与心理咨询的一体化服务。')],mistakes:[m("The integrated systems was tested before launch.","The integrated systems were tested before launch.","The plural subject systems requires the plural verb were.")],quiz:[q('integrated',1,1,'An integrated system is one whose parts?','are joined to work together as a whole','are kept completely unrelated','have all been removed','integrated 表示合并成为一个整体的。'),q('integrated',2,1,'An integrated course combines history, art, and science. The subjects are?','brought together in a connected program','taught without any links between them','replaced by a single exam score','整合课程把多个内容联系起来。'),q('integrated',3,1,'Choose the closest meaning.','unified','separated','unfinished','unified 表示统一、合为一体。'),q('integrated',4,1,'Which phrase is most natural?','an integrated transport network','an integrated collection of disconnected parts','an integrated system with nothing joined','integrated 常修饰被整合为整体的系统或服务。')]});
D('integrity',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪中期来自拉丁语 integritatem（integritas 的宾格），意为‘完整、健全、正直’，源自 integer‘完整的、未受损的’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/integrity"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"科研 · 诚信","senseId":"integrity.s1","en":"The reviewer praised the analyst's integrity because she reported the failed trials alongside the successful results instead of hiding inconvenient data.","zh":"审稿人赞扬分析师为人正直，因为她同时报告失败和成功的试验结果，而没有隐瞒不利数据。","structure":"The reviewer praised the analyst's integrity / because she reported the failed trials alongside the successful results / instead of hiding inconvenient data.","grammar":"integrity 指诚实守原则；instead of + -ing 表示选择不做某事。","rationale":"她如实披露所有结果，体现 s1 的正直诚信。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The engineers tested the dam’s structural integrity after the earthquake.','地震后，工程师检测了大坝的结构完整性。')],mistakes:[m('She showed integrity by lying about her qualifications to get the job.','She showed dishonesty by lying about her qualifications to get the job.','靠谎报资历获职体现不诚实，而非 integrity（正直）；改为 dishonesty。')],quiz:[q('integrity',1,1,'A person of integrity is?','honest and guided by strong moral principles','willing to lie whenever it is useful','unable to make a decision','sense 1 指正直、诚实和道德操守。'),q('integrity',2,2,'A bridge loses structural integrity when?','its structure is no longer whole or sound','its engineers demonstrate honesty','its paint color changes','sense 2 指结构完整性或完好状态。'),q('integrity',3,1,'Which phrase refers to moral character?','personal integrity','structural integrity','territorial integrity','personal integrity 指个人操守和正直。'),q('integrity',4,2,'A wall’s integrity is in doubt after cracks appear. Its?','soundness may have been damaged','honesty has been questioned','intelligence has increased','建筑语境中的 integrity 指完整、健全程度。')]});
D('intellect',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪末经古法语 intellect 来自拉丁语 intellectus‘理解、认识’，源自 intellegere‘理解、辨别’，与 inter‘在……之间’和 legere‘选择、阅读’相关。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intellect"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"教育 · 推理","senseId":"intellect.s1","en":"The puzzle challenged her intellect because every clue mattered, yet the solution depended on noticing how two apparently unrelated events were connected.","zh":"这个谜题考验了她的智力，因为每条线索都很重要，而解法取决于能否发现两个看似无关的事件之间的联系。","structure":"The puzzle challenged her intellect / because every clue mattered / yet the solution depended on noticing how two apparently unrelated events were connected.","grammar":"challenge one's intellect 表示考验智力；depend on + -ing 表示取决于做某事。","rationale":"解题需要推理和理解能力，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The philosopher was a leading intellect whose essays shaped public debate.','这位哲学家是影响公共讨论的杰出知识分子。')],mistakes:[m("She used her intellect to reasoning through the difficult proof.","She used her intellect to reason through the difficult proof.","The infinitive marker to is followed by the base verb reason, not the gerund reasoning.")],quiz:[q('intellect',1,1,'A problem that requires intellect calls for?','reasoning and understanding','physical strength alone','memorizing a color without thinking','sense 1 指推理和理解的思维能力。'),q('intellect',2,2,'“One of the great intellects of her time” describes?','a person with an exceptionally strong mind','a musical instrument from that period','a person hired to inspect buildings','sense 2 可数名词指才智出众的人。'),q('intellect',3,1,'Which noun focuses most on reasoning ability?','intellect','insurance','instruction','intellect 尤指思考、推理和理解能力。'),q('intellect',4,2,'The newspaper called the scientist a public intellect. It called the scientist?','a prominent thinker','a monthly payment','a government inspector','intellect 可借指知识分子或有才智的人。')]});
D('intellectual',{
    etymology: {"origin":"来自拉丁语 intellectualis，源自 intellectus‘理解、认识’，而 intellectus 与 intellegere‘辨别、理解’有关；形容词义涉及思考和理解能力。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intellectual"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"健康 · 认知","senseId":"intellectual.s1","en":"The assessment measures intellectual development through age-appropriate reasoning tasks, while teachers also observe how children solve problems during ordinary play.","zh":"这项评估通过适龄推理任务衡量智力发展，教师也会观察孩子在日常游戏中如何解决问题。","structure":"The assessment measures intellectual development through age-appropriate reasoning tasks / while teachers also observe / how children solve problems during ordinary play.","grammar":"intellectual 修饰 development，表示与思考理解能力有关；while 连接两种评估方式。","rationale":"语境关注推理和解决问题的脑力能力，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(3,'The magazine invited several intellectuals to debate the future of public libraries.','这本杂志邀请了几位知识分子讨论公共图书馆的未来。')],mistakes:[m("Their conversation was intellectual ideas about education.","Their conversation was about intellectual ideas about education.","The adjective intellectual modifies ideas; the preposition about is needed to connect the conversation to its topic.")],quiz:[q('intellectual',1,1,'Intellectual development concerns?','the growth of thinking and understanding','the growth of muscle size only','the installation of a computer','sense 1 是与智力、思考能力有关的。'),q('intellectual',2,2,'An intellectual conversation is likely to involve?','serious ideas and thoughtful discussion','only loud music and no exchange of ideas','a routine building inspection','sense 2 描写喜欢严肃思想、善于思考的交流。'),q('intellectual',3,3,'A public intellectual is?','a thinker who engages with public ideas','a person who only repairs instruments','an official who issues insurance policies','sense 3 可数名词指知识分子或思想者。'),q('intellectual',4,1,'Which phrase describes mental rather than physical work?','intellectual challenge','physical injury','monthly instalment','intellectual 常与思维、脑力活动相关。')]});
D('intelligence',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪末经古法语 intelligence 或直接来自拉丁语 intelligentia，源自 intelligentem（intellegere‘理解、辨别’的现在分词），指理解和学习能力。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intelligence"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"教育 · 学习能力","senseId":"intelligence.s1","en":"The study found that intelligence is not measured by one test alone, because learning also depends on practice, health, and access to good teaching.","zh":"研究发现，智力不能只靠一次测试衡量，因为学习还取决于练习、健康状况和获得优质教学的机会。","structure":"The study found that intelligence is not measured by one test alone / because learning also depends on practice / health, and access to good teaching.","grammar":"intelligence 指理解和学习能力；be measured by 表示通过某方法衡量。","rationale":"研究讨论的是学习与理解能力，而非情报信息，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The assessment measures problem-solving ability as one aspect of intelligence.','这项测评把解决问题的能力作为智力的一个方面来衡量。')],mistakes:[m('The test measures intelligence, which is each participant’s shoe size.','The test measures intelligence, which is each participant’s ability to learn and reason.','鞋码是身体尺寸，不是智力；改成学习和推理能力的说明。')],quiz:[q('intelligence',1,1,'A test of intelligence aims to measure a person’s?','ability to learn, understand, and think','height and shoe size','amount of money saved','intelligence 指学习、理解和思考的能力。'),q('intelligence',2,1,'The test measures intelligence. In this sentence intelligence is?','an uncountable noun','a plural noun that always takes -s','a verb describing an action','来源条目将 intelligence 标为不可数名词。'),q('intelligence',3,1,'Which word is closest in meaning?','intellect','inlet','intake','intellect 与 intelligence 都涉及智力或思维能力。'),q('intelligence',4,1,'A person’s intelligence may help them?','learn new concepts and solve problems','open an air intake','pay an insurance premium','理解和解决问题体现智力。')]});
D('intelligent',{
    etymology: {"origin":"来自拉丁语 intelligentem（intellegere‘理解、辨别’的现在分词）；英语形容人或机器时，分别可指善于学习思考或能处理信息。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intelligent"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"科技 · 设备","senseId":"intelligent.s2","en":"The intelligent thermostat learns when the building is occupied and lowers heating automatically, but staff can still override it during a cold snap.","zh":"这款智能温控器会学习建筑何时有人，并自动降低供暖；但寒潮期间工作人员仍可手动覆盖设置。","structure":"The intelligent thermostat learns when the building is occupied / and lowers heating automatically / but staff can still override it during a cold snap.","grammar":"intelligent 修饰 thermostat，表示设备能根据输入信息作出响应；when 引导宾语从句。","rationale":"设备会根据占用情况调整运行，符合 s2 的智能机器义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The intelligent thermostat learns the household schedule and adjusts the heating.','这款智能恒温器会学习家庭作息并调节供暖。')],mistakes:[m('She is intelligent because she cannot learn from feedback or understand a simple explanation.','She is unintelligent because she cannot learn from feedback or understand a simple explanation.','无法从反馈中学习、也不能理解简单解释与 intelligent（聪明的）相反。')],quiz:[q('intelligent',1,1,'An intelligent student is usually able to?','learn and think effectively','avoid understanding every lesson','operate only by following a timer','sense 1 指学习、理解和思考能力强。'),q('intelligent',2,2,'An intelligent braking system can?','process information and respond automatically','play a melody on a musical instrument','insure a driver against every possible loss','sense 2 指能以似乎有思考的方式处理信息的智能机器。'),q('intelligent',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym for an intelligent child.','bright','insincere','insolvent','bright 可表示聪明、悟性好。'),q('intelligent',4,2,'Which phrase uses the technical sense?','an intelligent traffic-control system','an intelligent moral principle','an intelligent monthly payment','智能交通系统体现机器处理信息并响应的义项。')]});
D('intelligible',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪末来自拉丁语 intelligibilis‘可理解的’，源自 intelligere‘理解、辨别’；该词形容表达清楚到能够被听懂或读懂。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intelligible"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"沟通 · 说明","senseId":"intelligible.s1","en":"The guide gave an intelligible explanation of the evacuation route, using plain language and a clear map for visitors who had just arrived.","zh":"导览员用浅白的语言和清晰地图解释了疏散路线，让刚到访的游客能够理解。","structure":"The guide gave an intelligible explanation of the evacuation route / using plain language and a clear map / for visitors who had just arrived.","grammar":"intelligible 修饰 explanation；using 分词结构说明解释清楚的方式。","rationale":"游客能够理解路线说明，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The lecturer rewrote the proof in intelligible language for first-year students.','讲师把证明改写成大一学生能理解的表达。')],mistakes:[m('The announcement was intelligible, but nobody could understand a single word of it.','The announcement was unintelligible, so nobody could understand a single word of it.','没人能听懂任何一个词说明内容不可理解；加 un- 表示反义。')],quiz:[q('intelligible',1,1,'An intelligible recording is?','clear enough to be understood','so faint that no words can be recognized','intended only for a different speaker','sense 1 指能被听懂或理解的。'),q('intelligible',2,2,'A speaker makes an argument intelligible by?','expressing it clearly','using unexplained jargon throughout','removing every link between ideas','sense 2 强调表达清晰、意思明白。'),q('intelligible',3,1,'Which word is closest in meaning?','understandable','intelligent','insignificant','understandable 表示可理解；intelligent 表示聪明，意义不同。'),q('intelligible',4,1,'If a message is barely intelligible, it is?','just possible to understand','perfectly clear to everyone','impossible to send','barely intelligible 表示勉强能听懂或理解。')]});
D('intend',{
    etymology: {"origin":"约1300年经古法语 entendre/intendre 来自拉丁语 intendere‘把注意力指向、伸向’，由 in-‘朝向’与 tendere‘伸展’构成；‘计划做’义在14世纪末已有。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intend"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"项目 · 计划","senseId":"intend.s1","en":"We intend to finish the roof repairs before winter, but the schedule allows extra days in case the replacement tiles arrive late.","zh":"我们打算在冬天前完成屋顶维修，但日程留有额外时间，以防替换瓦片迟到。","structure":"We intend to finish the roof repairs before winter / but the schedule allows extra days / in case the replacement tiles arrive late.","grammar":"intend to do 表示打算做某事；in case 引出预防性安排。","rationale":"说话者有完成维修的计划，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The gift was intended for new volunteers who had completed the training.','这份礼物是送给完成培训的新志愿者的。'),ex(3,'I did not intend “cheap” as criticism; I meant that the repair was affordable.','我说“便宜”不是批评，而是想表达维修费用负担得起。')],mistakes:[m('The note was intended for new staff, but it was prepared specifically for them.','The note was not intended for new staff, but it was prepared specifically for them.','专门为新员工准备的说明正是 intended for them；补 not 才能与前半句一致。')],quiz:[q('intend',1,1,'I intend to leave before sunset. I?','plan to leave before sunset','have already left before sunset','was forced to stay until morning','sense 1 指打算或计划做某事。'),q('intend',2,2,'The guide is intended for first-time visitors. It is?','designed or meant for those visitors','written by visitors after their trip','a guide that must not be used by visitors','be intended for 表示专为某人或用途准备。'),q('intend',3,3,'“That is not what I intended” means?','that was not the meaning I wanted to express','I planned to say exactly those words','I want the listener to repeat the sentence','sense 3 指说话者原本想表达的意思。'),q('intend',4,1,'Which pattern is correct?','intend to apply','intend for apply','intend at applying to','intend to do 是表示计划的常用结构。')]});
D('intended',{
    etymology: {"origin":"intended 是 intend 的过去分词形容词；intend 经古法语来自拉丁语 intendere‘把注意力指向、计划’，表示某事是有意安排的。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intend"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"沟通 · 误解","senseId":"intended.s1","en":"The intended message was a friendly reminder, but its blunt wording sounded like an order when the team read it during a stressful shift.","zh":"原本想表达的是友善提醒，但团队在紧张的轮班期间读到这段生硬措辞时，却觉得像命令。","structure":"The intended message was a friendly reminder / but its blunt wording sounded like an order / when the team read it during a stressful shift.","grammar":"intended 修饰 message，表示原本计划表达的内容；but 对比意图与实际效果。","rationale":"信息内容是有意设计的提醒，符合 s1 的‘有意的’义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The intended audience for the safety leaflet is parents of young children.','这份安全宣传单的目标读者是幼儿家长。')],mistakes:[m('The damage was intended because the driver struck the barrier by accident while trying to avoid it.','The damage was unintended because the driver struck the barrier by accident while trying to avoid it.','意外碰撞不是有意造成的；加 un- 改为 unintended。')],quiz:[q('intended',1,1,'An intended effect is one that?','was planned or wanted','happened entirely by accident','was impossible to predict and never considered','intended 表示有意计划或希望出现的。'),q('intended',2,1,'The intended audience for a children’s book is?','the readers it was designed for','everyone who has never learned to read','the people who printed the book','intended audience 指预定读者群。'),q('intended',3,1,'If the result was not intended, it was?','not planned on purpose','carefully designed in advance','the only outcome the team wanted','not intended 是否定“有意计划”。'),q('intended',4,1,'Choose the natural phrase.','the intended use of the tool','the use intendedly of the tool','the intend use of the tool','intended 可作形容词修饰 use。')]});
D('intense',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪中期经法语 intense 来自拉丁语 intensus，是 intendere 的过去分词形式，含‘拉紧、集中’之意；英语形容程度、情绪或专注非常强烈。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intend"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"天气 · 现象","senseId":"intense.s1","en":"The intense heat lasted through the night, forcing the crew to stop outdoor work and move the temperature-sensitive equipment indoors.","zh":"酷热持续了一整夜，迫使工作人员停止户外作业，并把对温度敏感的设备移到室内。","structure":"The intense heat lasted through the night / forcing the crew to stop outdoor work / and move the temperature-sensitive equipment indoors.","grammar":"intense 修饰 heat，表示程度极高；forcing 分词短语说明结果。","rationale":"热度达到极高程度，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The interview became intense when both candidates challenged each other’s claims.','两位候选人互相质疑对方说法时，面试气氛变得紧张。'),ex(3,'He is an intense reader who thinks deeply about every novel.','他读书投入而认真，会深入思考每一部小说。')],mistakes:[m('The pain was intense, but the patient described it as mild and barely noticeable.','The pain was mild, and the patient described it as barely noticeable.','剧烈疼痛不可能同时轻微到几乎察觉不到；把 intense 换为 mild。')],quiz:[q('intense',1,1,'Intense pain is pain that is?','very strong','slight and barely noticeable','felt only after the pain has ended','sense 1 表示程度非常强烈。'),q('intense',2,2,'An intense look may show?','strong feeling or concentration','complete lack of attention','an official safety inspection','sense 2 可形容情感或注意力高度集中。'),q('intense',3,3,'An intense person is someone who?','feels things deeply and seriously','avoids caring about any subject','works only for a few seconds','sense 3 描写感受深、投入度高的人。'),q('intense',4,1,'Which phrase refers to very great degree?','intense heat','intensive farming','an intended audience','intense heat 中 intense 表示酷热、程度强。')]});
D('intensify',{
    etymology: {"origin":"1817年由 intense 加 -ify 构成，意为‘使更强或变得更强’；英语早期另有 intensen 等形式，现代词形以 intensify 为主。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intend"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"天气 · 变化","senseId":"intensify.s1","en":"Winds are expected to intensify after sunset, so the harbor authority moved small boats to protected moorings before crews went home.","zh":"预计日落后风力会增强，因此港务部门在船员回家前把小船移到了避风泊位。","structure":"Winds are expected to intensify after sunset / so the harbor authority moved small boats to protected moorings / before crews went home.","grammar":"intensify 作不及物动词，表示风力变强；be expected to 表示预计。","rationale":"风逐渐增强，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The wind intensified overnight, forcing the ferry service to stop.','风势夜间增强，渡轮服务被迫停运。')],mistakes:[m('As the storm moved away, the wind intensified and became steadily weaker.','As the storm moved away, the wind weakened and became steadily weaker.','intensify 表示增强，与 steadily weaker 相反；改为 weakened。')],quiz:[q('intensify',1,1,'If a storm intensifies, it?','becomes stronger','disappears without changing','moves to a different season','intensify 表示变得更强或加剧。'),q('intensify',2,1,'Heavy rain intensified the flooding. The rain?','made the flooding worse','stopped all water from rising','repaired the damaged road','及物用法表示使洪水等情况加剧。'),q('intensify',3,1,'Which word is closest in meaning?','escalate','diminish','relax','escalate 也表示升级或加剧。'),q('intensify',4,1,'The debate intensified after new evidence appeared. The debate became?','more forceful or serious','less active and completely over','a written instruction manual','不及物 intensify 表示争论变得更激烈。')]});
D('intensity',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 intense 加名词后缀 -ity 构成；intense 来自拉丁语 intensus（intendere 的过去分词），与拉紧、集中或程度增强的意象相关。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intense"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"运动 · 训练","senseId":"intensity.s1","en":"The coach reduced the intensity of the session when several athletes reported dizziness, then increased the workload gradually over the next month.","zh":"几名运动员报告头晕后，教练降低了训练强度，并在接下来一个月逐步增加负荷。","structure":"The coach reduced the intensity of the session / when several athletes reported dizziness / then increased the workload gradually over the next month.","grammar":"the intensity of + 活动表示其强度；reduce/increase 对照强度变化。","rationale":"描述训练有多强烈，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The camera automatically adjusts the light intensity in a dark room.','相机会在暗室中自动调节光线强度。')],mistakes:[m("The intensity of the warning signals were measured overnight.","The intensity of the warning signals was measured overnight.","The head noun intensity is singular, so it takes was despite the plural noun signals in the of-phrase.")],quiz:[q('intensity',1,1,'The intensity of a light describes?','how strong or powerful it is','how many lamps are in the room','the color printed on the lamp','intensity 指强度或力量的大小。'),q('intensity',2,1,'High-intensity sound may be?','very loud or powerful','almost impossible to hear','a count of musical instruments','高强度描述声音或信号力量大。'),q('intensity',3,1,'Which adjective forms the noun intensity?','intense','intelligent','intangible','intensity 是 intense 的名词形式。'),q('intensity',4,1,'“Light of high intensity” means light that?','is extremely strong','comes from only one bulb','has no measurable brightness','high intensity 指强光或强度很大。')]});
D('intensive',{
    etymology: {"origin":"15世纪中期经古法语 intensif 或中世纪拉丁语 intensivus 来自拉丁语 intensus（intendere 的词干），表示程度很高、集中投入的。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intense"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"教育 · 短期课程","senseId":"intensive.s1","en":"The intensive language course meets every morning for three weeks, combining conversation practice, reading assignments, and daily feedback from tutors.","zh":"这门强化语言课程连续三周每天上午上课，结合会话练习、阅读任务和导师每日反馈。","structure":"The intensive language course meets every morning for three weeks / combining conversation practice, reading assignments / and daily feedback from tutors.","grammar":"intensive 修饰 course，表示短期内投入大量学习；combining 分词说明课程内容。","rationale":"课程在短时间内安排密集工作，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The farm uses intensive methods and a large amount of labor on each hectare.','这家农场采用集约化方法，每公顷投入大量劳动力。'),ex(3,'Doctors moved him to intensive care after the operation.','手术后，医生将他转入重症监护。')],mistakes:[m('The intensive course covered one short lesson per month with almost no study between classes.','The intensive course covered several hours of study each day with little free time.','短期内高强度投入才是 intensive course 的特点；每月一节且几乎不学习不符合。')],quiz:[q('intensive',1,1,'An intensive language course usually involves?','a lot of study in a short period','one brief class each year','no practice or homework','sense 1 指短时间内投入大量学习或工作。'),q('intensive',2,2,'Labour-intensive farming uses?','a large amount of human labor','almost no workers or resources','only a written instruction sheet','sense 2 指大量使用劳动等资源的集约型生产。'),q('intensive',3,3,'A patient in intensive care receives?','very thorough and closely monitored medical care','a short sightseeing tour','a series of monthly payments','来源的第三义强调照护深入、密集。'),q('intensive',4,1,'Which phrase is correct?','an intensive training program','an intense care unit','an intensifying class in one month','常见搭配是 intensive training 或 intensive care。')]});
D('intent',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪末经古法语 entent 或直接来自拉丁语 intentus‘专注、伸向’，源自 intendere‘伸展、集中注意’；名词 intent 表示计划或目的。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intend"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"行动 · 动机","senseId":"intent.s1","en":"The guard's intent was to protect the collection, so she checked each visitor's badge without delaying families at the entrance.","zh":"保安的意图是保护藏品，因此她检查每位访客的证件，同时没有让入口处的家庭久等。","structure":"The guard's intent was to protect the collection / so she checked each visitor's badge / without delaying families at the entrance.","grammar":"intent 作名词表示目的；intent was to do 说明计划要做的事。","rationale":"句中直接说明保安行动的目的，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The court found that the driver had entered the restricted area with intent to steal equipment.','法院认定司机进入限制区域的意图是盗窃设备。')],mistakes:[m('His intent was to return the wallet, and he planned to keep it for himself.','His intent was to return the wallet, and he planned to give it back.','归还钱包与据为己有矛盾；把 keep it for himself 改为 give it back。')],quiz:[q('intent',1,1,'“His intent was to help” tells us his?','purpose or plan','physical strength','ability to understand a lecture','intent 指计划或意图。'),q('intent',2,1,'A person who acted with intent did so?','on purpose','without any awareness','only after being carried there','with intent 常表示蓄意或有目的地。'),q('intent',3,1,'Which phrase is natural in a legal context?','with intent to deceive','with intentionly deceive','with intent of deceive to','with intent to do something 是常见搭配。'),q('intent',4,1,'The word intent in “his intent was clear” is a?','noun naming a purpose','verb meaning to inspect','plural adjective describing tools','此句中 intent 作名词“意图”。')]});
D('intention',{
    etymology: {"origin":"14世纪初经古法语 entencion 或直接来自拉丁语 intentionem，源自 intendere‘把注意力指向、伸展’，名词表示计划或打算。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intend"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"社交 · 解释","senseId":"intention.s1","en":"I had no intention of excluding Maya from the meeting; the calendar invitation simply failed to include her updated address.","zh":"我并无意把玛雅排除在会议之外；只是日历邀请没有包含她更新后的地址。","structure":"I had no intention of excluding Maya from the meeting / the calendar invitation simply failed / to include her updated address.","grammar":"have no intention of + -ing 表示无意做某事；failed to do 表示未能做到。","rationale":"说话者说明自己没有排除玛雅的计划，符合 s1。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'Her intention was to keep the community garden open to everyone.','她的打算是让社区花园继续向所有人开放。')],mistakes:[m('He had no intention of apologizing, but he planned to apologize as soon as they met.','He had every intention of apologizing, and he planned to do so as soon as they met.','明确计划见面后道歉与“无意道歉”相矛盾；改为 every intention。')],quiz:[q('intention',1,1,'A person’s intention is their?','plan or purpose','monthly insurance payment','ability to reason','intention 指打算或计划。'),q('intention',2,1,'“I had no intention of offending you” means?','I did not plan or mean to offend you','I planned carefully to offend you','I do not know what an offense is','no intention of 表示没有做某事的打算。'),q('intention',3,1,'Which phrase is standard?','with the intention of helping','with intention to of helping','intention for helpingly','常用结构是 with the intention of + 名词或动名词。'),q('intention',4,1,'His good intentions were clear. The phrase refers to his?','good purposes or plans','intelligence test results','official instructions','intention 的复数 intentions 可指用意或计划。')]});
D('intentional',{
    etymology: {"origin":"由 intention 加形容词后缀 -al 构成；intention 经古法语或直接来自拉丁语 intentionem，源自 intendere‘把注意力指向、计划’。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/intention"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"调查 · 事故","senseId":"intentional.s1","en":"The investigators concluded that the damaged cable was not intentional, because the maintenance log showed it had worn through during ordinary use.","zh":"调查人员认定电缆损坏并非故意造成，因为维修记录显示它是在正常使用中磨损断裂的。","structure":"The investigators concluded that the damaged cable was not intentional / because the maintenance log showed / it had worn through during ordinary use.","grammar":"intentional 作表语，表示有意造成；not intentional 否定故意性。","rationale":"证据显示损坏不是有意行为，正好体现 s1 的故意义。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(1,'The referee judged the handball to be intentional after reviewing the replay.','裁判查看回放后判定这次手球是故意的。')],mistakes:[m('The spill was intentional because she dropped the glass by accident while turning away.','The spill was unintentional because she dropped the glass by accident while turning away.','意外失手不是有意所为；加 un- 表示非故意。')],quiz:[q('intentional',1,1,'An intentional action is done?','on purpose','by accident','without anyone taking action','intentional 表示故意、有意做的。'),q('intentional',2,1,'An intentional foul in a match is?','a deliberate violation','a harmless accident with no contact','a legal instruction from the referee','故意犯规是 deliberate foul。'),q('intentional',3,1,'Choose the closest synonym.','deliberate','accidental','insufficient','deliberate 与 intentional 都表示故意的。'),q('intentional',4,1,'If the mistake was not intentional, it was?','accidental','planned','deliberate','not intentional 表示并非故意，即意外发生。')]});
D('interact',{
    etymology: {"origin":"1805年由 inter-‘相互、在……之间’与 act（行动）构成，意为彼此作用或互相影响；名词 interact 另有幕间节目等专门义。","prefix":null,"root":null,"suffix":null,"source":"Etymonline — https://www.etymonline.com/word/interact"},
    contexts: [{"domain":"化学 · 反应","senseId":"interact.s2","en":"These two medicines can interact in the body, changing how quickly each is absorbed, so the pharmacist checked the patient's full prescription list.","zh":"这两种药物可能在体内相互作用，改变各自的吸收速度，因此药剂师核对了患者的完整处方清单。","structure":"These two medicines can interact in the body / changing how quickly each is absorbed / so the pharmacist checked the patient's full prescription list.","grammar":"interact 可表示两种事物彼此产生影响；how quickly 引导间接疑问从句。","rationale":"一种药物改变另一种药物的吸收过程，符合 s2。","sourceType":"authored"}],extraExamples:[ex(2,'The two medicines may interact, so the pharmacist checked the combination.','这两种药可能相互作用，因此药剂师检查了它们的组合。')],mistakes:[m('The children interacted with one another by refusing to speak or take part in any shared activity.','The children remained separate from one another by refusing to speak or take part in any shared activity.','不交谈也不共同参与活动说明没有互动；改为 remained separate。')],quiz:[q('interact',1,1,'Children interact with classmates when they?','talk or do activities together','avoid all contact with them','read alone in another building','sense 1 指与他人交流或一起做事。'),q('interact',2,2,'Two drugs interact when they?','affect each other when used together','are taken by unrelated patients years apart','are stored in separate buildings','sense 2 指事物彼此产生影响。'),q('interact',3,1,'Which preposition often follows interact?','with','by of','at from to','常见搭配是 interact with。'),q('interact',4,1,'A student who never speaks or works with classmates does not?','interact much with them','insulate them from criticism','instruct them in mathematics','互动义 interact 涉及与他人交往或合作。')]});
